 Pursuant to § 240.14a-12\n28  Providence and Worcester Railroad Company \n29  (Name of Registrant as Specified In Its Charter) \n30  Not Applicable \n31  (Name of\n32 Person(s) Filing Proxy Statement, if other than the Registrant) \n33  Payment of Filing Fee (Check the appropriate box): \n34  ¨ \n35  No fee required.\n36  ¨ \n37  Fee computed on table below per Exchange Act Rules 14a-6(i)(1) and 0-11. \n38  (1)\n39  Title of each class of securities to which transaction applies:\n40  (2) \n41  Aggregate number of securities to which transaction applies:\n42  (3)\n43  Per unit price or other underlying value of transaction computed pursuant to Exchange Act Rule 0-11 (set forth the amount on which the\n44 filing fee is calculated and state how it was determined):\n45  (4)\n46  Proposed maximum aggregate value of transaction: \n47  (5)\n48  Total fee paid: \n49  x \n50  Fee paid previously with preliminary materials.\n51  ¨ \n52  Check box if any part of the fee is offset as provided by Exchange Act Rule 0-11(a)(2) and identify the filing for which the offsetting fee was paid previously. Identify the previous filing by regist\n53 number, or the form or schedule and the date of its filing.\n54  (1)\n55  Amount previously paid:\n56  (2)\n57  Form, Schedule or Registration Statement no.:\n58  (3)\n59  Filing Party:\n60  (4)\n61  Date Filed:\n62  Table of Contents \n63  Your vote is very important. \n64  September 19, 2016 \n65  Dear Shareholder: \n66  On August 12, 2016, Providence and Worcester Railroad Company (“PWRR” or the “Company”) entered into a merger agreement\n67 among the Company, Genesee & Wyoming Inc. (“G&W”) and Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc. (“Merger Sub”), providing for the acquisition of the Company by G&W through the merger of Merger Sub with and into th\n68 “merger”), with the Company surviving the merger. If completed, the merger will result in the Company becoming a wholly-owned subsidiary of G&W. \n69  On behalf of the Company’s board of directors (the “Board”), you are cordially invited to attend a special meeting of\n70 shareholders, which will be held at Union Station, Two Washington Square, Worcester, Massachusetts 01604, on Wednesday, October 26, 2016 at 10:00 a.m., local time. At the special meeting, you will be \n71 approve the merger agreement and the merger. At the special meeting, you will also be asked to vote on (1) a proposal to approve, on an advisory (non-binding) basis, the compensation that may be paid \n72 executive officers in connection with, or following the completion of, the merger, (2) a proposal to adjourn the special meeting if necessary to permit further solicitation of proxies if there are not\n73 meeting to approve the merger agreement, and (3) any other business properly brought before the special meeting and any adjournment or postponement thereof. \n74  If the merger agreement is approved and the merger is subsequently completed, (i) each outstanding share of PWRR preferred stock, par value\n75 $50.00 per share (the “preferred stock”), other than preferred stock held by a holder who is entitled to and makes a proper demand for dissenters’ rights, will be deemed to be automatically converted,\n76 or accumulated and unpaid dividends thereon, into 100 shares of PWRR common stock, par value $0.50 per share (the “common stock”) without any further action by the holders of such preferred stock, and\n77 and outstanding at the effective time of the merger (including common stock into which the preferred stock has been deemed converted, but excluding common stock owned by G&W or any of its direct or in\n78 shall, as of the effective time of the merger, be converted into and exchanged for the right to receive cash in the amount of $25.00, without interest, per share of common stock, less any applicable w\n79  The merger cannot be completed unless holders of a majority of the shares of preferred stock and a majority of the shares of common stock\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"TITLE: DEFM14A\nLINES: 5782\nCHARS: 623416\n0  \n1  DEFM14A\n2  1\n3  d224035ddefm14a.htm\n4  DEFM14A\n5  DEFM14A \n6  Table of Contents \n7  UNITED STATES \n8  SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION \n9  Washington, D.C. 20549 \n10  SCHEDULE 14A\n11 INFORMATION \n12  Proxy Statement Pursuant to Section 14(a) of the \n13  Securities Exchange Act of 1934 \n14  Filed by the\n15 Registrant x Filed by\n16 a Party other than the Registrant ¨ \n17  Check the appropriate box: \n18  ¨ \n19  Preliminary Proxy Statement\n20  ¨ \n21  Confidential, for Use of the Commission only (as permitted by Rule 14a-6(e)(2)) \n22  x \n23  Definitive Proxy Statement\n24  ¨ \n25  Definitive Additional Materials\n26  ¨ \n27  Soliciting Material Pursuant to § 240.14a-12\n28  Providence and Worcester Railroad Company \n29  (Name of Registrant as Specified In Its Charter) \n30  Not Applicable \n31  (Name of\n32 Person(s) Filing Proxy Statement, if other than the Registrant) \n33  Payment of Filing Fee (Check the appropriate box): \n34  ¨ \n35  No fee required.\n36  ¨ \n37  Fee computed on table below per Exchange Act Rules 14a-6(i)(1) and 0-11. \n38  (1)\n39  Title of each class of securities to which transaction applies:\n40  (2) \n41  Aggregate number of securities to which transaction applies:\n42  (3)\n43  Per unit price or other underlying value of transaction computed pursuant to Exchange Act Rule 0-11 (set forth the amount on which the\n44 filing fee is calculated and state how it was determined):\n45  (4)\n46  Proposed maximum aggregate value of transaction: \n47  (5)\n48  Total fee paid: \n49  x \n50  Fee paid previously with preliminary materials.\n51  ¨ \n52  Check box if any part of the fee is offset as provided by Exchange Act Rule 0-11(a)(2) and identify the filing for which the offsetting fee was paid previously. Identify the previous filing by regist\n53 number, or the form or schedule and the date of its filing.\n54  (1)\n55  Amount previously paid:\n56  (2)\n57  Form, Schedule or Registration Statement no.:\n58  (3)\n59  Filing Party:\n60  (4)\n61  Date Filed:\n62  Table of Contents \n63  Your vote is very important. \n64  September 19, 2016 \n65  Dear Shareholder: \n66  On August 12, 2016, Providence and Worcester Railroad Company (“PWRR” or the “Company”) entered into a merger agreement\n67 among the Company, Genesee & Wyoming Inc. (“G&W”) and Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc. (“Merger Sub”), providing for the acquisition of the Company by G&W through the merger of Merger Sub with and into th\n68 “merger”), with the Company surviving the merger. If completed, the merger will result in the Company becoming a wholly-owned subsidiary of G&W. \n69  On behalf of the Company’s board of directors (the “Board”), you are cordially invited to attend a special meeting of\n70 shareholders, which will be held at Union Station, Two Washington Square, Worcester, Massachusetts 01604, on Wednesday, October 26, 2016 at 10:00 a.m., local time. At the special meeting, you will be \n71 approve the merger agreement and the merger. At the special meeting, you will also be asked to vote on (1) a proposal to approve, on an advisory (non-binding) basis, the compensation that may be paid \n72 executive officers in connection with, or following the completion of, the merger, (2) a proposal to adjourn the special meeting if necessary to permit further solicitation of proxies if there are not\n73 meeting to approve the merger agreement, and (3) any other business properly brought before the special meeting and any adjournment or postponement thereof. \n74  If the merger agreement is approved and the merger is subsequently completed, (i) each outstanding share of PWRR preferred stock, par value\n75 $50.00 per share (the “preferred stock”), other than preferred stock held by a holder who is entitled to and makes a proper demand for dissenters’ rights, will be deemed to be automatically converted,\n76 or accumulated and unpaid dividends thereon, into 100 shares of PWRR common stock, par value $0.50 per share (the “common stock”) without any further action by the holders of such preferred stock, and\n77 and outstanding at the effective time of the merger (including common stock into which the preferred stock has been deemed converted, but excluding common stock owned by G&W or any of its direct or in\n78 shall, as of the effective time of the merger, be converted into and exchanged for the right to receive cash in the amount of $25.00, without interest, per share of common stock, less any applicable w\n79  The merger cannot be completed unless holders of a majority of the shares of preferred stock and a majority of the shares of common stock\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Command exited with code 0."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /home/uctpiaj/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport re, html\\nraw = open('raw_filing/providence-worcester_2016-09-20_DEFM14A.htm', encoding='utf-8', errors='replace').read()\\n# print title and header bits\\nm = re.search(r'<title[^>]*>(.*?)</title>', raw, re.S|re.I)\\nprint(\\\"TITLE:\\\", m.group(1) if m else None)\\ntext = re.sub(r'(?is)<(script|style).*?</\\\\1>', ' ', raw)\\n# replace block tags with newlines\\ntext = re.sub(r'(?i)<br\\\\s*/?>', '\\\\n', text)\\ntext = re.sub(r'(?i)</(p|div|tr|table|h1|h2|h3|h4|li|td)>', '\\\\n', text)\\ntext = re.sub(r'(?s)<[^>]+>', ' ', text)\\ntext = html.unescape(text)\\ntext = text.replace('\\\\xa0',' ')\\ntext = re.sub(r'[ \\\\t]+', ' ', text)\\ntext = re.sub(r'\\\\n\\\\s*\\\\n+', '\\\\n', text)\\nopen('/tmp/opencode/pxw_text.txt','w').write(text)\\nlines = text.split('\\\\n')\\nprint(\\\"LINES:\\\", len(lines))\\nprint(\\\"CHARS:\\\", len(text))\\nfor i,l in enumerate(lines[:80]):\\n    print(i, l[:200])\\nEOF\"}"},"time":{"start":1789824297118,"end":1789824298145}}}}
