nce coverage exceed such amount, G&W and the Company will be obligated to obtain a policy with the greatest coverage available for a cost not exceeding such amount. In lieu\n1802:above, provided that the premium is not more than 300% of the annual premium paid by the Company for such insurance on the date of the merger agreement. \n2297:expend in any one year an amount in excess of 300% of the annual premium paid by the Company for such insurance on the date of the merger agreement. If the annual premiums for such insurance coverage exceed such amount, G&W and the Company will\n2299:“tail” insurance coverage that provides coverage identical in all material respects to the coverage described above, provided that the premium is not more than 300% of the annual premium paid by the Company for such insurance on the date\n2658: MARKET PRICE OF COMMON STOCK \n3686:premiums due the Pension Benefit Guaranty Corporation (which premiums have been paid when due). With respect to each Title IV Plan set forth on Section 3.13(a) of the Company Disclosure Letter that is not a Multiemployer Plan:\n4315:in any one year an amount in excess of 300% of the annual premiums currently paid by the Company for such insurance, which annual premiums currently paid are set forth on Section 5.9(b) of the Company Disclosure Letter (the “ Maximum\n4316:Premium ”); and provided , further , that, if the annual premiums for such insurance coverage exceed the Maximum Premium, Parent and the Surviving Corporation will be obligated to obtain a policy with the greatest coverage\n4318:“tail” insurance coverage that provides coverage identical in all material respects to the coverage described above, provided that the Company does not pay more than the Maximum Premium. \n4355:its Subsidiaries’ properties and assets securing its obligations under its existing credit facilities and any historic credit facilities or other historic financing (to the extent Encumbrances under such historic facilities or other financing\n4787:receipts, property, sales, use, license, excise, franchise, employment, payroll, premium, withholding, alternative or added minimum, ad valorem, transfer or excise tax, social security or tax relating to compensation or benefits provided to\n4984: Maximum Premium\n5476: reviewed certain information relating to the historical, current and future operations, financial condition and prospects of the Company made available to us by the Company, including financial projections prepared by\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"294: MARKET PRICE OF COMMON STOCK \n667: Market Price of Our Common Stock (page 71)\n669:the NASDAQ on August 12, 2016, which was the last trading day before we announced the merger, was $16.30. On September 16, 2016, the last trading day before the date of this proxy statement, the closing price of Company common stock on the NASDAQ\n1342:current market price of the Company’s common stock and the historical, present and anticipated future operating results and financial position of the Company;\n1347: the fact that the value of the merger consideration of $25.00 per share in cash represents a 53% premium over the per share closing price of the Company’s common stock of $16.30 on August 12, 2016, the last trading\n1465: reviewed certain information relating to our historical, current and future operations, financial condition and\n1545:their respective closing prices on August 11, 2016, and were based on the most recent publicly available information and Street consensus estimates. The selected companies were as follows: \n1710:should be evaluated, if at all, in conjunction with the historical financial statements and other information regarding the Company contained in the Company’s public filings with the SEC. \n1799:the merger. Neither G&W nor the surviving corporation will be obligated to expend in any one year an amount in excess of 300% of the annual premium paid by the Company for such insurance on\n1800:the date of the merger agreement. If the annual premiums for such insurance coverage exceed such amount, G&W and the Company will be obligated to obtain a policy with the greatest coverage available for a cost not exceeding such amount. In lieu\n1802:above, provided that the premium is not more than 300% of the annual premium paid by the Company for such insurance on the date of the merger agreement. \n2297:expend in any one year an amount in excess of 300% of the annual premium paid by the Company for such insurance on the date of the merger agreement. If the annual premiums for such insurance coverage exceed such amount, G&W and the Company will\n2299:“tail” insurance coverage that provides coverage identical in all material respects to the coverage described above, provided that the premium is not more than 300% of the annual premium paid by the Company for such insurance on the date\n2658: MARKET PRICE OF COMMON STOCK \n3686:premiums due the Pension Benefit Guaranty Corporation (which premiums have been paid when due). With respect to each Title IV Plan set forth on Section 3.13(a) of the Company Disclosure Letter that is not a Multiemployer Plan:\n4315:in any one year an amount in excess of 300% of the annual premiums currently paid by the Company for such insurance, which annual premiums currently paid are set forth on Section 5.9(b) of the Company Disclosure Letter (the “ Maximum\n4316:Premium ”); and provided , further , that, if the annual premiums for such insurance coverage exceed the Maximum Premium, Parent and the Surviving Corporation will be obligated to obtain a policy with the greatest coverage\n4318:“tail” insurance coverage that provides coverage identical in all material respects to the coverage described above, provided that the Company does not pay more than the Maximum Premium. \n4355:its Subsidiaries’ properties and assets securing its obligations under its existing credit facilities and any historic credit facilities or other historic financing (to the extent Encumbrances under such historic facilities or other financing\n4787:receipts, property, sales, use, license, excise, franchise, employment, payroll, premium, withholding, alternative or added minimum, ad valorem, transfer or excise tax, social security or tax relating to compensation or benefits provided to\n4984: Maximum Premium\n5476: reviewed certain information relating to the historical, current and future operations, financial condition and prospects of the Company made available to us by the Company, including financial projections prepared by\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Command exited with code 0."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /tmp/opencode && grep -n -i \\\"premium\\\\|unaffected\\\\|market price\\\\|closing price\\\\|52-week\\\\|historic\\\" pxw_text.txt | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1789824401370,"end":1789824401674}}}}
