\n1286 31 meeting of the Transaction Committee, the Board held a special meeting to review\n1294 31 that the draft merger agreement and disclosure letter for both Party B and G&W h\n1302 32 Party B indicated that it would not increase its price.\n1304 32 the request of the Board, representatives of BMO reviewed BMO’s financial analys\n1314 32 G&W executed the merger agreement, and the Company, G&W and the Eder Trusts exec\n1317 32 merger agreement and voting agreement, representatives of BMO advised the Board \n1319 32 6, 2016, the Board considered this new information, determined this relationship\n1339 33 •\n1347 33 day concluded prior to the Company and G&W entering into the merger agreement;\n1672 41 engagement letter with the Company and in three monthly installments thereafter,\n1679 42 Facility Agreement dated as of March 20, 2015 under which an affiliate of BMO is\n2659 71 the high and low sale prices per share for our common stock as reported on the N\n2739 71 approximately 540 holders of record of common stock and 640 shares of preferred \n2751 72 842,742 shares of common stock and 500 shares of preferred stock. Under the voti\n4681 A-48 Parent dated April 3, 2016.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"n markers: 133\n1161 27 Vice President and Chief Commercial Officer) met with one of the Company’s Class\n1175 27 based upon its examination of these and other factors, that it was in the best i\n1185 28 senior management team of the Company met with various representatives of Party \n1190 28 interest in a change in control transaction. During the week of March 28, 2016, \n1192 28 prohibit a potential buyer from submitting a proposal or making an offer to acqu\n1194 28 representatives of GHF and members of the Company’s management held a series of \n1198 28 Convention. Mr. Noreck reported that the Company had also approached two additio\n1201 28 With the assistance of GHF