{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789824901564,"sessionID":"ses_f4628b113ffe9gyXGlLM5DZwK2","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e0a0610019bBHMQsdKKfW2c","sessionID":"ses_f4628b113ffe9gyXGlLM5DZwK2","messageID":"msg_0b9df3655001JeXfbf7QuNIWSA","type":"tool","id":"call_01_HlUeyjq2v2SNKwwcGZvn6896","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode && sed -n '1338,1348p' pxw_text.txt; echo ...; sed -n '1540,1545p' pxw_text.txt; echo ...; sed -n '1582,1594p' pxw_text.txt"},"output":" the fact that the Company conducted a lengthy and thorough process, directed by the Board and the Transaction Committee, during which the Board sought offers to purchase from a broad group of potential bidders,\nincluding strategic and financial buyers, 25 of whom entered into confidentiality agreements with the Company and received information related to the Company and six of whom submitted non-binding letters of intent; \n •\n the review by the Board with the Company’s management and advisors of the structure of the merger and the financial and other terms of the merger agreement, including the merger consideration in relation to the\ncurrent market price of the Company’s common stock and the historical, present and anticipated future operating results and financial position of the Company;\n •\n based on the Board’s review of the process conducted by the Transaction Committee, the Board’s belief that $25.00 per share in cash and the terms of the merger agreement offer the best value reasonably\nattainable for the Company’s shareholders; \n •\n the fact that the value of the merger consideration of $25.00 per share in cash represents a 53% premium over the per share closing price of the Company’s common stock of $16.30 on August 12, 2016, the last trading\nday concluded prior to the Company and G&W entering into the merger agreement; \n...\n Selected Publicly Traded Companies Analysis \n BMO reviewed and compared certain publicly available financial information, ratios and market multiples relating to the Company with equivalent\npublicly available data for companies that share similar business characteristics with the Company to derive an implied equity value reference range for the Company. BMO reviewed seven publicly traded North American freight railroads companies. BMO\nanalyzed the ratio of enterprise value (which we refer to as EV) to earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization (which we refer to as EBITDA) for each of the last twelve months as of June 30, 2016 (which we refer to as LTM) and\nfor estimated calendar year 2016 based on consensus Wall Street analyst research (which we refer to as Street consensus) for each of these companies for comparison purposes. The multiples for each of the selected companies were calculated using\ntheir respective closing prices on August 11, 2016, and were based on the most recent publicly available information and Street consensus estimates. The selected companies were as follows: \n...\n This analysis indicated the following implied per share equity value reference range for each\nshare of the Company’s common stock, as compared to the consideration to be received by the Company’s common shareholders in the merger: \n Implied Per Share Equity Value Reference Range \n EV/LTM\nEBITDA \n EV/2016E \n EBITDA \n Merger \n Consideration \n $10.95 - $14.56 \n $11.42 - $15.09 \n $25.00\n No company utilized in the selected publicly traded companies analysis is identical to the Company. In\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":" the fact that the Company conducted a lengthy and thorough process, directed by the Board and the Transaction Committee, during which the Board sought offers to purchase from a broad group of potential bidders,\nincluding strategic and financial buyers, 25 of whom entered into confidentiality agreements with the Company and received information related to the Company and six of whom submitted non-binding letters of intent; \n •\n the review by the Board with the Company’s management and advisors of the structure of the merger and the financial and other terms of the merger agreement, including the merger consideration in relation to the\ncurrent market price of the Company’s common stock and the historical, present and anticipated future operating results and financial position of the Company;\n •\n based on the Board’s review of the process conducted by the Transaction Committee, the Board’s belief that $25.00 per share in cash and the terms of the merger agreement offer the best value reasonably\nattainable for the Company’s shareholders; \n •\n the fact that the value of the merger consideration of $25.00 per share in cash represents a 53% premium over the per share closing price of the Company’s common stock of $16.30 on August 12, 2016, the last trading\nday concluded prior to the Company and G&W entering into the merger agreement; \n...\n Selected Publicly Traded Companies Analysis \n BMO reviewed and compared certain publicly available financial information, ratios and market multiples relating to the Company with equivalent\npublicly available data for companies that share similar business characteristics with the Company to derive an implied equity value reference range for the Company. BMO reviewed seven publicly traded North American freight railroads companies. BMO\nanalyzed the ratio of enterprise value (which we refer to as EV) to earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization (which we refer to as EBITDA) for each of the last twelve months as of June 30, 2016 (which we refer to as LTM) and\nfor estimated calendar year 2016 based on consensus Wall Street analyst research (which we refer to as Street consensus) for each of these companies for comparison purposes. The multiples for each of the selected companies were calculated using\ntheir respective closing prices on August 11, 2016, and were based on the most recent publicly available information and Street consensus estimates. The selected companies were as follows: \n...\n This analysis indicated the following implied per share equity value reference range for each\nshare of the Company’s common stock, as compared to the consideration to be received by the Company’s common shareholders in the merger: \n Implied Per Share Equity Value Reference Range \n EV/LTM\nEBITDA \n EV/2016E \n EBITDA \n Merger \n Consideration \n $10.95 - $14.56 \n $11.42 - $15.09 \n $25.00\n No company utilized in the selected publicly traded companies analysis is identical to the Company. In\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Command exited with code 0."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /tmp/opencode && sed -n '1338,1348p' pxw_text.txt; echo ...; sed -n '1540,1545p' pxw_text.txt; echo ...; sed -n '1582,1594p' pxw_text.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1789824901218,"end":1789824901564}}}}
