(3 wks)',\n    rel='revises R036')\n# --- selection\nqs, m, off = quotes(('P-020', 'The Transaction Committee concluded that the Company should proceed with confirmatory due diligence', 'relative to the other potential buyers'),\n                    ('P-020', 'representatives of GHF subsequently contacted the remaining bidders', 'no longer involved in the process'),\n                    ('P-020', 'Director Smith is Vice President', 'potential buyer of the Company'))\nadd(when='07/27/2016', who='Transaction Committee (in person after the regular quarterly Board meeting)',\n    what='Target decision', rnd='2', typ=None,\n    terms='Concluded that the Company should proceed with confirmatory due diligence and negotiations with G&W and Party B because of their higher offers, and directed that the remaining bidders be told they were no longer involved; independent directors updated (Director Smith recused because GATX Corporation, which he serves and which holds 4.92% of the common stock, might be a potential buyer).',\n    why='Target decision (stated): selection of two finalists and exclusion of the rest in one shared decision. Quotes: \\u201c'+qs[0]+'\\u201d / \\u201c'+qs[1]+'\\u201d / \\u201c'+qs[2]+'\\u201d',\n    src=['P-020'], review='Q1', df='2016-07-27', dt='2016-07-27', wa='2016-07-27',\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported', rel='closes R023; drops R039\\u2013R042; R043')\nfor who, typ, rid_ in [('Party C','Strategic','R024'), ('Party D','Financial','R030'),\n                       ('Party E','Strategic','R029'), ('Party F','Strategic','R032')]:\n    q, m, off = quotes(('P-020', 'representatives of GHF subsequently contacted the remaining bidders', 'no longer involved in the process'))\n    add(when='after 07/27/2016; day not disclosed', who=who, what='Dropped by target', rnd='2', typ=typ,\n        terms='Told after the 07/27/2016 selection that it was no longer involved in the process; stage left: Round 2 (the selection stage); Decided by: Target; Exit reason: Lower offer than rivals (the higher offers of G&W and Party B).',\n        why='Dropped by target (stated as to the group; individual identification of the remaining bidders is by their LOI participation \\u2014 all six LOI submitters except G&W and Party B). Quote: \\u201c'+q+'\\u201d The notification is undated and follows the decision; assigned to the decision day.',\n        src=['P-020'], review=None, count=1, df=None, dt='2016-07-27', wa='2016-07-27',\n        basis='Relative only', method='Assigned: decision day', dec='Target', ex='Lower offer than rivals',\n        ob='Stated', rel='selection R038; earlier bid '+rid_)\n# --- Round 3\nqs, m, off = quotes(('P-020', 'proceed with confirmatory due diligence and negotiations with G&W and Party B', 'higher offers made by each of G&W and Party B'),\n                    ('P-022', 'From July 27, 2016 through August 11, 2016', 'track infrastructure'))\nadd(when='07/27/2016', who='Process (Round 3)', what='Round opened', rnd='3', typ=None,\n    terms='Confirmatory due diligence and definitive negotiation with selected bidders (G&W and Party B): on-site financial, legal and environmental diligence including hi-rail track inspections (07/27\\u201308/11/2016); revised merger agreement and voting agreement to Party B (08/01/2016) and G&W (08/03/2016); Party B prioritized from 08/04/2016. Round finality: Inferred final \\u2014 the target moved to definitive negotiation with the selected bidders at this round\\u2019s opening and concluded with the executed 08/12/2016 agreement; no further solicitation. Alternative boundary 08/04 or 08/12 rejected (Q1).',\n    why='Round opened (section 6.3: the target moves to definitive negotiation with selected bidders). Quotes: \\u201c'+qs[0]+'\\u201d / \\u201c'+qs[1]+'\\u201d',\n    src=['P-020','P-022'], review='Q1', df='2016-07-27', dt='2016-07-27', wa='2016-07-27',\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported', rfin='Inferred final', rel='candidates: 08/04/2016, 08/12/2016 (rejected)')\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-021', 'On July 29, 2016', 'reengaging and enhancing their offers'))\nfor who, typ, nxt in [('Party D','Financial','R046'), ('Party E','Strategic','R047')]:\n    add(when='07/29/2016', who=who, what='Re-entered', rnd='3', typ=typ,\n        terms='Renewed participation after the 07/27/2016 exclusion: on a GHF call, '+who+' expressed interest in reengaging and enhancing its offer; revised LOI followed on 08/01/2016 ('+nxt+'). Decided by: Bidder; renewed activity, not a new NDA. Count 1.',\n        why='Re-entered (stated): renewed activity after a recorded departure (section 10.1). Quote: \\u201c'+q+'\\u201d',\n        src=['P-021'], review='Q4', count=1, df='2016-07-29', dt='2016-07-29', wa='2016-07-29',\n        basis='Reported day', method='Reported', dec='Bidder', ob='Stated', rel='reopens after R039/R040')\nqs, m, off = quotes(('P-021', 'On August 1, 2016, Party D submitted a revised LOI', '$24.00 per share'),\n                    ('P-021', 'Both revised proposals contained a 30-day due diligence period', '30-day due diligence period'),\n                    ('P-021', 'Party D declined to shorten its due diligence period', 'during its 30-day due diligence period'))\nadd(when='08/01/2016', who='Party D', what='Bid', rnd='3', typ='Financial',\n    terms='Revised LOI at $24.00 per share (as-converted; point) with a 30-day due diligence period (up from four weeks); on 08/02/2016 also requested that the Company commit not to enter an agreement with another bidder during that period (request declined). First Party D bid in Round 3 (Count 1).',\n    why='Bid (stated price revision). Quotes: \\u201c'+qs[0]+'\\u201d / \\u201c'+qs[1]+'\\u201d Exclusivity request: \\u201c'+qs[2]+'\\u201d Formality: carried forward from Party D\\u2019s returned mark-ups (section 9.2, one continuing proposal) \\u2192 Formal. Conditions: stated 30-day diligence period and the later no-sign demand \\u2192 Heavy.',\n    src=['P-021'], review='Q6', count=1, df='2016-08-01', dt='2016-08-01', wa='2016-08-01',\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported', pl=24.00, ph=24.00, kind='Point', origin='Stated',\n    curr='USD', cash='Not stated',\n    cdetail='Fin: not stated; DD required: substantive (30 days); DD open: yes; Excl: requested (30 days)',\n    rel='revises R030; excluded R039, re-entered R044')\nqs, m, off = quotes(('P-021', 'Party E submitted a revised LOI', '$23.81 per share'),\n                    ('P-021', 'Both revised proposals contained a 30-day due diligence period', '30-day due diligence period'))\nadd(when='08/01/2016', who='Party E', what='Bid', rnd='3', typ='Strategic',\n    terms='Support: Party F (financing) \\u2014 revised LOI at $23.81 per share (as-converted; point) with a 30-day due diligence period, submitted along with financing support from Party F (which had exited on 07/27/2016; no re-entry row and no independent bid by Party F after its exit). First Party E bid in Round 3 (Count 1).',\n    why='Bid (stated price revision with a disclosed financing-support relationship; section 5.3 records support on the supported bidder\\u2019s offer row). Quotes: \\u201c'+qs[0]+'\\u201d / \\u201c'+qs[1]+'\\u201d Formality: carries forward Party E\\u2019s Informal status (issues summary; no markup returned) \\u2014 flag Q6. Conditions: 30-day diligence period \\u2192 Heavy.',\n    src=['P-021'], review='Q6', count=1, df='2016-08-01', dt='2016-08-01', wa='2016-08-01',\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported', pl=23.81, ph=23.81, kind='Point', origin='Stated',\n    curr='USD', cash='Not stated',\n    cdetail='Fin: not stated; DD required: substantive (30 days); DD open: yes; Excl: not stated',\n    rel='revises R029; supporter exited at R042 (no re-entry); support ended with R048')\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-021', 'confirmed its original proposal of $21.26 per share', '$21.26 per share'))\nadd(when='08/02/2016', who='Party E', what='Bid', rnd='3', typ='Strategic',\n    terms='Reverted to its original proposal: withdrew the revised $23.81 LOI and confirmed the original proposal of $21.26 per share (the financing support for the withdrawn revised proposal ended); a bid reversion, not a process withdrawal; second Party E bid in Round 3, so Count 0.',\n    why='Bid reversion (stated; section 9.1 keeps reversions as Bid rows). Quote: \\u201c'+q+'\\u201d Formality: Informal (as R029). Conditions: original proposal\\u2019s 60-day exclusivity/diligence terms stand \\u2192 Heavy.',\n    src=['P-021'], review='Q6', count=0, df='2016-08-02', dt='2016-08-02', wa='2016-08-02',\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported', pl=21.26, ph=21.26, kind='Point', origin='Stated',\n    curr='USD', cash='Not stated',\n    cdetail='Fin: not stated; DD required: substantive (60 days); DD open: yes; Excl: requested (60 days)',\n    rel='reverts to R029; supersedes R047')\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-021', 'Party D declined to shorten its due diligence period', 'at that time'))\nadd(when='08/02/2016', who='Party D', what='Withdrew', rnd='3', typ='Financial',\n    terms='Declined to shorten its 30-day due diligence period and requested a commitment that the Company not enter an agreement with another bidder during that period; in light of the active interest of Party B and G&W the Company declined to commit, at which point Party D indicated it would not proceed with further due diligence at that time. Decided by: Bidder; Exit reason: Terms or process.',\n    why='Withdrew (stated): the bidder communicates it will not continue participating. Quote: \\u201c'+q+'\\u201d The reason is process/terms (refused shorter diligence and the no-sign commitment), stated by the bidder.',\n    src=['P-021'], review='Q4', count=1, df='2016-08-02', dt='2016-08-02', wa='2016-08-02',\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported', dec='Bidder', ex='Terms or process', ob='Stated')\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-023', 'G&W requested that it be allowed to continue its due diligence', 'which request was granted'),\n                   ('P-023', 'On August 11, 2016, G&W indicated', 'physical diligence of the Company'))\nadd(when='08/09/2016\\u201308/11/2016', who='G&W', what='Material process update', rnd='3', typ='Strategic',\n    terms='Continued due diligence granted to G&W: after the 08/09/2016 decision directing BMO to tell G&W that the Company intended to enter a merger agreement with another bidder, G&W requested continued due diligence to potentially facilitate an improved offer; the request was granted and G&W completed physical diligence on 08/10\\u201308/11/2016, then indicated a possible revised LOI for 08/12/2016. Precise action: access/continued diligence granted to a rival after the target\\u2019s selection of Party B.',\n    why='Material process update (stated): consequential development with no more specific label; it changed the competitive information position that produced G&W\\u2019s 08/12/2016 bid. Quotes: \\u201c'+q[0]+'\\u201d / \\u201c'+q[1]+'\\u201d',\n    src=['P-023'], review='Q1', df='2016-08-09', dt='2016-08-11', wa='2016-08-09',\n    basis='Reported interval', method='Assigned: bound')\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-023', 'representatives of Hinckley Allen and Simpson', 'legal counsel'))\nadd(when='08/10/2016', who='Simpson Thacher & Bartlett LLP (Simpson Thacher) \\u2014 G&W legal counsel',\n    what='Adviser service observed', rnd='3', typ=None,\n    terms='G&W\\u2019s legal counsel; first shown acting 08/10/2016 (discussed merger agreement and voting agreement provisions with Hinckley Allen and received a revised disclosure letter); engagement date not disclosed.',\n    why='Adviser service observed (stated): the filing shows Simpson Thacher acting; no engagement date. Quote: \\u201c'+q+'\\u201d',\n    src=['P-023'], review=None, df='2016-08-10', dt='2016-08-10', wa='2016-08-10',\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported')\nqs, m, off = quotes(('P-024', 'G&W submitted a revised LOI to acquire the Company', 'on the following'))\nadd(when='08/12/2016 (morning)', who='G&W', what='Bid', rnd='3', typ='Strategic',\n    terms='Revised LOI at $25.00 per share in cash (as-converted; point), dropping the previously proposed CVR, together with mark-ups of the merger agreement and voting agreement; offer stated to expire 6:00 p.m. on 08/13/2016; submitted after G&W completed physical diligence and after the Company told G&W it intended to sign with another bidder; first G&W bid in Round 3 (Count 1).',\n    why='Bid (stated final price revision). Quote: \\u201c'+qs[0]+'\\u201d Formality: returned agreement and voting-agreement markups + price confirmation in definitive negotiation \\u2192 Formal. Conditions: diligence completed 08/11/2016, no diligence or exclusivity condition attached, no Heavy trigger reported \\u2192 Light (financing silent; silence does not raise or lower the level; None not claimed because financing is not stated). All cash: Yes; cash at closing $25.00.',\n    src=['P-024'], review='Q6; Q8', count=1, df='2016-08-12', dt='2016-08-12', wa='2016-08-12',\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported', pl=25.00, ph=25.00, kind='Point', origin='Stated',\n    curr='USD', cash='Yes', cclose=25.00,\n    cdetail='Fin: not stated; DD required: none; DD open: no; Excl: none', rel='revises R037')\nqs, m, off = quotes(('P-026', 'representatives of BMO then contacted Party B', 'would not increase its price'),\n                    ('P-027', 'The Board determined that the G&W offer represented the superior proposal', 'superior proposal'),\n                    ('P-027', 'Following a discussion of the terms of the merger agreement', 'plan of merger'))\nadd(when='08/12/2016 (afternoon; Transaction Committee met 10:30 a.m.)',\n    who='Board of Directors (special meeting; Director Smith recused)', what='Target decision', rnd='3', typ=None,\n    terms='After the Committee\\u2019s 10:30 a.m. meeting (BMO directed to inform Party B that a higher revised LOI had been received) and the Board\\u2019s comparison of the two drafts (G&W $1.00 per share higher; lower termination fee; STB approval timing not materially different; financing condition absent), the Board asked BMO to seek a higher price from Party B \\u2014 Party B declined; the Board determined G&W\\u2019s offer a superior proposal, received BMO\\u2019s oral fairness opinion (written opinion dated 08/12/2016, to holders other than the Eder Trusts) and approved the merger agreement and recommended shareholder approval.',\n    why='Target decision (stated). Quotes: \\u201c'+qs[0]+'\\u201d / \\u201c'+qs[1]+'\\u201d / \\u201c'+qs[2]+'\\u201d',\n    src=['P-026','P-027','P-029'], review='Q6', df='2016-08-12', dt='2016-08-12', wa='2016-08-12',\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported', rel='R052 (bid); R054 (signing); outcomes R055\\u2013R056')\nqs, m, off = quotes(('P-028', 'the Company and G&W executed the merger agreement', 'executed the voting agreement'),\n                    ('X-023', 'shall mean $3,785,000', '$3,785,000'))\nadd(when='08/12/2016', who='PWRR, G&W and Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc.', what='Merger agreement signed',\n    rnd='3', typ=None,\n    terms='Executed the merger agreement (Merger Sub merges into PWRR, which survives as a wholly owned G&W subsidiary; $25.00 cash per common share; preferred converted 100-for-1 plus accrued dividends; equity awards cashed out) and, with the Eder Trusts, the voting agreement (842,742 common / 500 preferred; ~17.3% / 78.1% of record-date class shares). Company termination fee $3,785,000 (~3% of transaction value; G&W draft negotiated down from 3.85%; Party B\\u2019s draft was 3% plus expenses capped at 1%); no financing condition; outside dates 12/31/2016, or 02/28/2017 if only STB approval remains. Signing is not a bid row: agreed consideration stated, price/formality cells left blank.',\n    why='Merger agreement signed (stated). Quotes: \\u201c'+qs[0]+'\\u201d / \\u201c'+qs[1]+'\\u201d Termination-fee and fiduciary-out terms were consequential for selection and are folded here (section 4).',\n    src=['P-028','X-023','X-010','P-026'], review='Q8', df='2016-08-12', dt='2016-08-12', wa='2016-08-12',\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported', rel='Board approval R053')\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-026', 'representatives of BMO then contacted Party B', 'would not increase its price'))\nadd(when='by 08/12/2016', who='Party B', what='Not selected at signing', rnd='3', typ='Strategic',\n    terms='Still bidding when the target chose another: standing $24.00 LOI; asked to improve and declined; target signed with G&W. Decided by: Target; Exit reason: Would not improve earlier offer. Outcome basis: Stated (the target chose another while Party B remained live).',\n    why='Not selected at signing (stated). Quote: \\u201c'+q+'\\u201d A bidder asked to improve and declining takes Would not improve earlier offer even though the target then chose the rival and Decided by is Target (section 10.3). No late-reconfirmation row is recorded for Party B: its latest priced row (R028) is Formal and sits in a round whose finality is Inferred final, so the section 9.1 test is not met.',\n    src=['P-026','P-028'], review='Q6', count=1, df=None, dt='2016-08-12', wa='2016-08-12',\n    basis='Relative only', method='Assigned: bound', dec='Target', ex='Would not improve earlier offer',\n    ob='Stated', rel='standing bid R028; signing R054')\nqs, m, off = quotes(('P-021', 'confirmed its original proposal of $21.26 per share', '$21.26 per share'),\n                    ('P-027', 'The Board determined that the G&W offer represented the superior proposal', 'superior proposal'))\nadd(when='by 08/12/2016', who='Party E', what='Not selected at signing', rnd='3', typ='Strategic',\n    terms='Still live when the target chose another: standing original proposal of $21.26 per share confirmed 08/02/2016; not chosen against G&W\\u2019s $25.00. Decided by: Target; Exit reason: Lower offer than rivals.',\n    why='Not selected at signing (stated). Quotes: \\u201c'+qs[0]+'\\u201d / \\u201c'+qs[1]+'\\u201d Party E was not displaced by exclusivity (none was executed), so this is a signing outcome, not an earlier withdrawal.',\n    src=['P-021','P-027','P-028'], review='Q4', count=1, df=None, dt='2016-08-12', wa='2016-08-12',\n    basis='Relative only', method='Assigned: bound', dec='Target', ex='Lower offer than rivals', ob='Stated',\n    rel='standing bid R048')\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-028', 'The Company issued a press release publicly announcing the transaction on Monday, August 15, 2016', 'opening of trading of'))\nadd(when='08/15/2016', who='PWRR (press release)', what='Merger announced', rnd='post', typ=None,\n    terms='Company press release publicly announcing the transaction on Monday, 08/15/2016 before the opening of NASDAQ trading; issuer: the Company; medium: press release. No go-shop, competing post-signing proposal, agreement termination or closing is disclosed in this filing.',\n    why='Merger announced (stated publicity). Quote: \\u201c'+q+'\\u201d',\n    src=['P-028'], review='Q1', df='2016-08-15', dt='2016-08-15', wa='2016-08-15',\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported')\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- sanity checks\nprev = None\nfor i, r in enumerate(rows, 1):\n    assert r['wa'] >= (prev or '0'), (i, r['wa'], prev)\n    prev = r['wa']\n    assert r['what'] != '', i\nprint('rows:', len(rows))\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- workbook\nwb = Workbook()\nLEDGER = 'Deal ledger'; SUMMARY = 'Summary'; QUESTIONS = 'Questions'; SOURCE = 'Source text'; LISTS = 'Lists'\n\nws = wb.active; ws.title = LEDGER\ngrp = {1:'Row identity', 17:'Count', 18:'Dates', 23:'Price', 28:'Settlement', 30:'Conditions detail',\n       31:'Deadline & round finality', 34:'Participation outcome', 37:'Source page', 38:'Related rows',\n       39:'Deal'}\nthin = Side(style='thin', color='BFBFBF')\nhdr_fill = PatternFill('solid', fgColor='1F3864')\nhdr_font = Font(bold=True, color='FFFFFF', size=10)\ngrp_fill = PatternFill('solid', fgColor='D9E1F2')\nfor c, name in enumerate(COLS, 1):\n    cell = ws.cell(row=2, column=c, value=name)\n    cell.font = hdr_font; cell.fill = hdr_fill; cell.alignment = Alignment(wrap_text=True, vertical='center')\n    if c in grp:\n        g = ws.cell(row=1, column=c, value=grp[c])\n        g.font = Font(bold=True, size=9, color='1F3864'); g.fill = grp_fill\n        g.alignment = Alignment(vertical='center')\n\ndef a1(c, r): return f'{get_column_letter(c)}{r}'\n\nsrc_rows = {}\nqrow = 2\nfor r in rows:\n    qrow += 1\n    main = r['src'][0]\n    if main not in src_rows:\n        raise SystemExit('unknown source id ' + main)\n    srow = src_rows[main]\n    vals = [qrow - 2, r['when'], r['who'], r['what'], 1, r['rnd'], r['typ'], r['terms'],\n            None, None, r['why'], None, r['review'], None,\n            f'R{qrow-2:03d}', 'Yes', r['count'], r['df'], r['dt'], r['wa'], r['basis'], r['method'],\n            r['pl'], r['ph'], r['kind'], r['origin'], r['curr'], r['cash'], r['cclose'],\n            r['cdetail'], r['due'], r['dlm'], r['rfin'], r['dec'], r['ex'], r['ob'],\n            None, r['rel'], DEAL]\n    for c, v in enumerate(vals, 1):\n        ws.cell(row=qrow, column=c, value=v)\nprint('ledger data rows:', qrow - 2)\n# styles\nwide = {2:20,3:30,4:19,5:8,6:7,7:11,8:70,9:11,10:12,11:95,12:34,13:9,14:14}\nfor c, w in wide.items():\n    ws.column_dimensions[get_column_letter(c)].width = w\nfor c in range(15, 40):\n    ws.column_dimensions[get_column_letter(c)].width = 14\nfor c in range(1, 40):\n    for rr in range(3, qrow + 1):\n        cell = ws.cell(row=rr, column=c)\n        cell.alignment = Alignment(wrap_text=(c in (2,3,4,8,11,12,14) or c >= 15),\n                                   vertical='top', shrink_to_fit=False)\nws.freeze_panes = 'D3'\nws.auto_filter.ref = f'A2:AM{qrow}'\n# expandable groups collapsed\nfor c in range(15, 40):\n    cd = ws.column_dimensions[get_column_letter(c)]\n    cd.outlineLevel = 1\n    cd.hidden = True\nws.sheet_properties.outlinePr.summaryRight = True\n# date number formats\nfor rr in range(3, qrow + 1):\n    for c in (18,19,20,31):\n        ws.cell(row=rr, column=c).number_format = 'mm/dd/yyyy'\n    for c in (23,24,29):\n        ws.cell(row=rr, column=c).number_format = '0.00'\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- source text sheet\nwss = wb.create_sheet(SOURCE)\nfor c, name in enumerate(['Paragraph','Section','Page','Text'], 1):\n    cell = wss.cell(row=1, column=c, value=name)\n    cell.font = hdr_font; cell.fill = hdr_fill; cell.alignment = Alignment(wrap_text=True, vertical='center')\nr = 1\nfor s in P_ROWS + X_ROWS:\n    r += 1\n    src_rows[s.sid] = r\n    wss.cell(row=r, column=1, value=s.sid)\n    wss.cell(row=r, column=2, value=s.section)\n    pg = s.page(0)\n    wss.cell(row=r, column=3, value=pg)\n    wss.cell(row=r, column=4, value=s.text)\nwss.column_dimensions['A'].width = 11\nwss.column_dimensions['B'].width = 46\nwss.column_dimensions['C'].width = 8\nwss.column_dimensions['D'].width = 150\nfor rr in range(2, r + 1):\n    wss.cell(row=rr, column=4).alignment = Alignment(wrap_text=True, vertical='top')\n    wss.cell(row=rr, column=1).alignment = Alignment(vertical='top')\n    wss.cell(row=rr, column=2).alignment = Alignment(wrap_text=True, vertical='top')\n    wss.cell(row=rr, column=3).alignment = Alignment(vertical='top')\nwss.freeze_panes = 'A2'\nwss.auto_filter.ref = f'A1:D{r}'\n\n# ledger Source hyperlinks + Review/Page\nfor i, rdata in enumerate(rows):\n    rr = 3 + i\n    main = rdata['src'][0]\n    lbl = '; '.join(rdata['src']) + ' (main: ' + main + ')'\n    f = f'=HYPERLINK(\"#{SOURCE}!$D${src_rows[main]}\",\"{lbl}\")'\n    ws.cell(row=rr, column=12, value=f)\n    ws.cell(row=rr, column=12).font = Font(color='0563C1', underline='single', size=9)\n    s = SRC[main]\n    qlist, m, off = quotes(*[(sid, must[0], must[1]) for (sid, must) in\n                             [(rdata['src'][0], (rdata['src'][0], rdata['src'][0]))]] ) if False else (None, None, None)\n    # page: page of first quote as recorded in why/reason via stored page below\n    ws.cell(row=rr, column=37, value=rdata.setdefault('page', None))\n\n# compute pages: re-locate first quote of each row by scanning the \"why\" cell for the source text\nfor i, rdata in enumerate(rows):\n    rr = 3 + i\n    reason = rdata['why']\n    page = None\n    for sid in rdata['src']:\n        s = SRC[sid]\n        # find the longest quoted fragment from s present in reason\n        best = None\n        for k in range(len(s.text) - 30):\n            frag = s.text[k:k+60]\n            if '\\u201d' in frag or '\\u201c' in frag:\n                continue\n            if frag in reason and (best is None or len(frag) > len(best[0])):\n                best = (frag, k)\n        if best:\n            page = s.page(best[1])\n            break\n    ws.cell(row=rr, column=37, value=page)\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Lists sheet\nwsl = wb.create_sheet(LISTS)\nLISTS_DEF = {\n 'What happened': ['Target interest','Bidder interest','Target sale decision','Activist pressure','Activist involvement',\n   'Adviser engaged','Adviser service observed','Adviser ended','Contact','NDA signed','Round opened','Deadline set',\n   'Deadline revised','Deadline','Target decision','Information access changed','Material process update',\n   'Exclusivity changed','Bid','Bid reaffirmed','Offer update','Other-scope bid','Valuation statement',\n   'Bidding group changed','Joined group','Dropped by target','Withdrew','Did not submit','Participation paused',\n   'Re-entered','Not selected at signing','Sale process announced','Bid announced','Merger announced',\n   'Merger agreement signed','Go-shop changed','Process terminated','Process restarted','Agreement terminated','Closed'],\n 'Type': ['Strategic','Financial','Mixed','Unknown'],\n 'Formality': ['Formal','Informal','Insufficient evidence','Varies'],\n 'Conditions level': ['None','Light','Heavy','Insufficient evidence','Varies'],\n 'Include': ['Yes','No'],\n 'Date basis': ['Reported day','Inferred day','Reported interval','Approximate window','Relative only','Undated'],\n 'Date method': ['Reported','Inferred','Assigned: deadline','Assigned: decision day','Assigned: midpoint','Assigned: bound','Assigned: sequence'],\n 'Price kind': ['Point','Bidder range','Group envelope','Bound only','Undisclosed'],\n 'Price origin': ['Stated','Carried forward','Inferred'],\n 'All cash': ['Yes','No','Not stated'],\n 'Deadline treatment': ['Extended','Extended; Late bids accepted','Late bids accepted','Enforced','Passed without action','Unclear','No deadline stated'],\n 'Round finality': ['Announced as final','Inferred final','Not final'],\n 'Decided by': ['Bidder','Target','Both','Unknown'],\n 'Exit reason': ['Value below market price','Value at or below market price','Value below earlier offer','Value at earlier offer',\n   'Would not improve earlier offer','Lower offer than rivals','Terms or process','Other stated reason','Not stated'],\n 'Outcome basis': ['Stated','Inferred: residual','Inferred: exclusivity','Inferred: silent','Inferred: identity'],\n}\nli = 0\nlist_ranges = {}\nfor name, vals in LISTS_DEF.items():\n    li += 1\n    col = get_column_letter(li)\n    c = wsl.cell(row=1, column=li, value=name); c.font = Font(bold=True)\n    for j, v in enumerate(vals, 2):\n        wsl.cell(row=j, column=li, value=v)\n    last = get_column_letter(li)\n    list_ranges[name] = f\"'{LISTS}'!${last}$2:${last}${len(vals)+1}\"\nwsl.sheet_state = 'hidden'\n\n# data validations\ndv_map = {'What happened': 4, 'Type': 7, 'Formality': 9, 'Conditions level': 10, 'Include': 16,\n          'Date basis': 21, 'Date method': 22, 'Price kind': 25, 'Price origin': 26, 'All cash': 28,\n          'Deadline treatment': 32, 'Round finality': 33, 'Decided by': 34, 'Exit reason': 35,\n          'Outcome basis': 36}\nfor name, col in dv_map.items():\n    dv = DataValidation(type='list', formula1=list_ranges[name], allow_blank=True,\n                        showErrorMessage=True, errorStyle='warning')\n    ws.add_data_validation(dv)\n    dv.add(f'{get_column_letter(col)}3:{get_column_letter(col)}{qrow}')\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Summary\nwsu = wb.create_sheet(SUMMARY, 1)\nwsu.column_dimensions['A'].width = 34\nwsu.column_dimensions['B'].width = 150\nrow = 1\ndef head(text):\n    global row\n    c = wsu.cell(row=row, column=1, value=text)\n    c.font = Font(bold=True, size=12, color='1F3864')\n    row += 1\ndef lbl(text, val, bold=False):\n    global row\n    a = wsu.cell(row=row, column=1, value=text); a.font = Font(bold=bold, size=10)\n    a.alignment = Alignment(wrap_text=True, vertical='top')\n    b = wsu.cell(row=row, column=2, value=val); b.alignment = Alignment(wrap_text=True, vertical='top')\n    row += 1\n\nt = wsu.cell(row=row, column=1, value='PWRR \\u00d7 G&W \\u2014 deal ledger summary (Providence and Worcester Railroad Company / Genesee & Wyoming Inc., 2016)')\nt.font = Font(bold=True, size=13); row += 1\nhead('1. Status and commercial account')\nlbl('Delivery status', 'AI first pass; not human-approved. Instruction: SEC_Deal_Ledger_Extraction_Instruction.md, revision of 19 September 2026 (short form). Supplied source: providence-worcester_2016-09-20_DEFM14A.htm \\u2014 PWRR definitive proxy statement (DEFM14A), filed 09/20/2016, proxy dated 09/19/2016. Source coverage: the complete \\u201cBackground of the Merger\\u201d (pp. 27\\u201332) is reproduced in order in the Source text sheet (P-001\\u2013P-029) with every other passage used (X-001 onward).')\nlbl('Commercial account', 'Initiation was mixed: a Q4 2015 approach by a Class I rail partner (Party A) expressing interest in acquiring equity led, through the Board\\u2019s banker search and its 03/14/2016 decision to explore a change of control, to a broad bank-run solicitation of 29 potential buyers (11 strategic, 18 financial) in the week of 03/28/2016. '\n    'Twenty-five buyers signed confidentiality agreements (no standstills); after introductory meetings and a memorandum, nine submitted non-binding IOIs received 05/19\\u201306/01/2016 at $17.93\\u2013$26.50 per share as-converted (equity values $90\\u2013134 million), and the committee excluded the two lowest and advanced seven to management presentations and a data site. '\n    'A mid-June solicitation for LOIs with agreement mark-ups (due 07/20/2016) produced six LOIs in late July at $19.20\\u2013$24.00: Party B ($24.00) and G&W ($21.15, then $22.15 including a $1.13 South Quay CVR) led; Party E ($21.26), Party D ($21.00), Party C ($19.30) and Party F ($19.20) followed; one strategic and one financial buyer elected not to submit. '\n    'On 07/27/2016 the committee chose G&W and Party B for confirmatory due diligence and definitive negotiation and told the remaining bidders they were out; Party D and Party E briefly re-engaged (08/01 revised LOIs of $24.00 and $23.81, Party E supported by Party F financing), but Party D withdrew on 08/02 after the Company declined a no-sign commitment and Party E reverted to $21.26. '\n    'On 08/12/2016 G&W\\u2019s final $25.00 all-cash LOI (CVR dropped, mark-ups returned, expiry 6:00 p.m. 08/13) displaced Party B\\u2019s $24.00 after Party B declined to raise, and the Board approved the merger agreement and the Eder Trusts\\u2019 voting agreement that same day. '\n    'Announcement followed on 08/15/2016; no go-shop, competing post-signing proposal, agreement termination or closing is disclosed, STB approval was pending (petition 09/01/2016; voting trust submission 09/14/2016), and closing was expected in Q4 2016.')\nhead('2. Deal facts')\nlbl('Target', 'Providence and Worcester Railroad Company (PWRR), a Rhode Island corporation; regional freight railroad in Massachusetts, Rhode Island, Connecticut and New York; NASDAQ: PWX; US public company. 4,866,593 common shares and 640 preferred shares outstanding on the 09/16/2016 record date (preferred convertible 100-for-1, non-cumulative $5.00 dividend).')\nlbl('Focal acquirer and type', 'Genesee & Wyoming Inc. (G&W), a Delaware corporation; NYSE: GWR; US public company; Strategic \\u2014 operating short-line/regional railroad acquirer, buying through its wholly owned shell Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc. (formed 08/12/2016).')\nlbl('Agreed consideration', '$25.00 per share in cash (as-converted basis: preferred deemed converted into 100 common shares plus accrued and unpaid dividends); equity awards cashed out at $25.00 (options net of exercise price; RSUs at $25.00); no financing condition; G&W representation as to financial wherewithal. All cash: Yes. No CVR in the signed terms.')\nlbl('Signing', '08/12/2016 \\u2014 merger agreement among PWRR, G&W and Merger Sub; voting agreement among PWRR, G&W and the Eder Trusts (842,742 common shares, 500 preferred shares).')\nlbl('Announcement', '08/15/2016 \\u2014 Company press release before the opening of NASDAQ trading.')\nlbl('Completion', 'Not observed in this filing (expected Q4 2016). Outside dates 12/31/2016, or 02/28/2017 if the only unsatisfied condition is STB approval. Expected closing kept separate from any observed closing.')\nlbl('Termination fee', '$3,785,000 payable by the Company to G&W in specified cases (~3% of transaction value; the Company negotiated G&W\\u2019s draft down from 3.85%; Party B\\u2019s draft was 3% plus its transaction expenses capped at 1%).')\nlbl('Filing identity and date', 'DEFM14A definitive proxy statement for the special meeting of shareholders (10/26/2016), filed 09/20/2016; background pages 27\\u201332. Source file: raw_filing/providence-worcester_2016-09-20_DEFM14A.htm.')\nhead('3. Process and round map')\nlbl('Processes', 'One sale process (Process 1). No earlier attempt is disclosed (the Q4 2015 Party A approach is round 0, not a separate process); no second process, go-shop or agreement termination is disclosed. Post-signing ledger content is publicity only (R057), with the STB process and the 09/06/2016 BMO conflict confirmation kept in these Summary blocks.')\nlbl('Round 0 (pre-solicitation)', 'R001 Party A interest (Q4 2015); R002 GHF adviser engaged (01/27/2016); R003 sale-strategy decision (03/14/2016); R004 Party A management meetings (03/22\\u201303/23); R005 contact authorization (03/24); R006 Hinckley Allen shown acting (03/24). No Round opened row for round 0.')\nlbl('Round 1 (week of 03/28 \\u2013 06/01/2016)', 'R008 anchor = first outreach wave \\u2014 29 potential buyers contacted (R007); rejected candidate anchors R003 and R005. NDA wave R009\\u2013R011 (25 signers: 10 strategic residual + 14 financial + G&W individually; no standstills). Access/differentiation: R012 (convention meetings), R013 (04/07 contact authorization), R014 (two additional Class I railroads contacted). Deadline history: R016 (05/10 set by 04/27), R017 (revised to 05/19), R018 (05/19; Enforced). Bids: R019 (nine IOIs, envelope $17.93\\u2013$26.50). Outcomes: R020 (16 residual non-submitters, inferred), R021 (06/01 decision), R022 (two low bidders dropped). Round-bidder tally: 9. Finality: Not final.')\nlbl('Round 2 (mid-June \\u2013 07/27/2016)', 'R023 opened the LOI stage (due 07/20/2016; mark-ups and draft documents posted to the data site 06/29\\u201307/11). Late entrant Party C: R024 NDA, R025 IOI ($21.00), R026 catch-up access. Bids: R028\\u2013R032 (B $24.00, E $21.26, D $21.00, C $19.30, F $19.20) and R036\\u2013R037 (G&W $21.15, then $22.15). Deadline: R027 (07/20; Late bids accepted). Outcomes: R033\\u2013R034 (two non-submitters), R035 (Party A identity row), R038 (07/27 selection of G&W and Party B), R039\\u2013R042 (C, D, E, F dropped). Round-bidder tally: 6. Finality: Inferred final.')\nlbl('Round 3 (07/27 \\u2013 08/12/2016)', 'R043 opened confirmatory due diligence and definitive negotiation with G&W and Party B. Re-entries R044\\u2013R045; bids R046\\u2013R048; withdrawal R049; access update R050; adviser R051; final bid R052 ($25.00); Board decision R053; signing R054; signing outcomes R055\\u2013R056. Round-bidder tally: 3. Finality: Inferred final.')\nlbl('Post-signing', 'R057 announcement (08/15/2016); no competing proposal, go-shop activity, agreement termination or closing observed. Regulatory: STB petition for exemption filed 09/01/2016 and voting-trust agreement submitted 09/14/2016 (X-009); outside dates X-010. Adviser conflict: on 09/06/2016 the Board considered BMO\\u2019s late disclosure of a ~5% BMO-affiliate lending participation in G&W\\u2019s secured syndicated facility and determined it was not material to BMO\\u2019s independence (P-029; X-016).')\nhead('4. Participants and advisers')\nlbl('G&W', 'Strategic (operating short-line/regional railroad; acquires through wholly owned shell Merger Sub). First observed 04/03/2016 (NDA R011; convention meeting R012); bids R036 ($21.15 with CVR), R037 ($22.15), R052 ($25.00 cash). Winner \\u2014 no exit row.')\nlbl('Party A', 'Strategic (Class I rail partner). First observed Q4 2015 (R001); NDA within R009; memorandum recipient; never mentioned again \\u2192 Count-0 identity row R035 (Inferred: identity; possible covers R033 recommended, R020, R022). See Q4/Q5.')\nlbl('Party B', 'Strategic. First individual meeting 04/21/2016 (R015); LOI R028 ($24.00); prioritized for definitive negotiation 08/04/2016; declined to raise on 08/12; Not selected at signing R055 (Would not improve earlier offer).')\nlbl('Party C', 'Strategic late entrant. NDA R024 (early July); IOI R025 ($21.00); LOI R031 ($19.30); dropped R039 (07/27).')\nlbl('Party D', 'Financial (as described in the filing). LOI R030 ($21.00); dropped R040; re-entered R044; revised LOI R046 ($24.00); Withdrew R049 (terms/process; no-sign commitment declined).')\nlbl('Party E', 'Strategic. LOI R029 ($21.26); dropped R041; re-entered R045; revised LOI R047 ($23.81 with Party F financing); reversion R048 ($21.26); Not selected at signing R056.')\nlbl('Party F', 'Strategic. LOI R032 ($19.20); dropped R042 (07/27 exit); provided financing support to Party E\\u2019s withdrawn 08/01 revised proposal (recorded on R047; no re-entry row after its exit).')\nlbl('Anonymous cohorts', 'Two unnamed low bidders (Unknown type; dropped R022); one unnamed strategic and one unnamed financial non-submitter (R033, R034); 16 residual NDA signers closed by inference at 05/19/2016 (R020); two additional Class I railroads contacted before 04/07/2016 that never entered (R014). Cohorts are not extra parties to add to their members.')\nlbl('Non-bidder holders', 'The Eder Trusts (shareholders; voting agreement 08/12/2016; X-012/X-024) and GATX Corporation (4.92% common holder; Director Smith recused from process meetings because GATX might be a potential buyer; no contact, NDA or bid disclosed) are not bidders and get no outcome rows.')\nlbl('Advisers', 'GHF (Greene Holcomb & Fisher LLC) \\u2192 BMO Capital Markets Corp. \\u2014 Company financial adviser; engaged 01/27/2016 (R002); GHF\\u2019s business acquired by BMO 08/01/2016 (same relationship); aggregate fee ~$2.52 million (X-015); BMO affiliate lending participation in G&W\\u2019s 2015 facility disclosed late and considered not material by the Board on 09/06/2016 (P-029; X-016). Hinckley, Allen & Snyder LLP \\u2014 Company legal counsel (R006; first shown acting 03/24/2016). Simpson Thacher & Bartlett LLP \\u2014 G&W legal counsel (R051; first shown acting 08/10/2016). The Company\\u2019s STB counsel is unnamed (P-026) and gets no adviser row. Disclosed attributes: PWRR and G&W are US public companies (NASDAQ: PWX; NYSE: GWR); ownership and country of the anonymous parties are not disclosed.')\nhead('5. Counts and auction screen')\nlbl('Auction screen', 'MET \\u2014 more than one independent prospective acquiring bidder unit executed bidder-target confidentiality agreements for this process (25 in the week-of-03/28 wave plus Party C; G&W among them). No lender-only, adviser or rollover-holder agreements are included; the Eder Trusts\\u2019 voting agreement is not a bidder NDA. Extraction proceeds regardless of the screen.')\nlbl('Contacts (ledger tally)', '31 from Contact rows (29 in the GHF outreach wave + 2 additional Class I railroads approached by the Company) plus 1 from the Party A Bidder interest row, which carries the Q4 2015 first contact = 32 contact units; Party A\\u2019s 03/22\\u201303/23 meeting and Party B\\u2019s 04/21 meeting are Count 0 repeats. Formula: ',\n    )\nws_formula_cell = None\nrow -= 1\nlbl('  \\u2192 formula', \"=SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\\\"Contact\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\"Yes\\\")+SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\\\"Bidder interest\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\"Yes\\\")\")\nlbl('  \\u2192 filing assertions', 'GHF contacted 11 potential strategic buyers and 18 potential financial buyers (29) in the week of 03/28/2016; the Company also approached two additional Class I railroads (P-004; P-006 \\u2014 X-002 reports a broad group without a number).')\nlbl('NDA signers (ledger tally)', \"=SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\\\"NDA signed\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\"Yes\\\")\")\nlbl('  \\u2192 filing assertions', 'Background: each of 11 potential strategic buyers and 14 potential financial buyers executed confidentiality agreements (25), plus Party C\\u2019s early-July agreement = 26 signatures on the ledger\\u2019s reading; the Board\\u2019s reasons state \\u201c25 of whom entered into confidentiality agreements\\u201d (X-002). Reconciliation in Q3: the reasons\\u2019 25 may exclude Party C or one strategic signer.')\nlbl('IOI submitters', '9 (stated; R019 cohort, envelope $17.93\\u2013$26.50). Filing: \\u201cnine written indications of interest\\u201d (P-008).')\nlbl('LOI submitters', '6 (stated; B, G&W, E, D, C, F \\u2014 R028\\u2013R032, R036; G&W\\u2019s 07/26 revision R037). Filing: \\u201csix LOIs\\u201d (P-012); group envelope $19.20\\u2013$24.00 / $96\\u2013121 million.')\nlbl('Round-bidder tallies', \"R1 = \" )\nrow -= 1\nlbl('  \\u2192 R1 / R2 / R3', \"=SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\\\"Bid\\\",'Deal ledger'!$F$3:$F$100,\\\"1\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\"Yes\\\")&\\\" / \\\"&SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\\\"Bid\\\",'Deal ledger'!$F$3:$F$100,\\\"2\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\"Yes\\\")&\\\" / \\\"&SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\\\"Bid\\\",'Deal ledger'!$F$3:$F$100,\\\"3\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\"Yes\\\")\")\nlbl('  \\u2192 scope', 'Bidder units newly represented as submitting in each round; not submissions and not unique bidders across the deal. R2 counts Party C\\u2019s IOI (R025) plus five LOIs; R3 counts D, E and G&W; later bids by the same bidder in the same round add 0 (G&W R037, C R031, E R048).')\nlbl('Exit units and inferred share', \"=SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$AI$3:$AI$100,\\\"<>\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\"Yes\\\")&\\\" exit units; \\\"&SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$AJ$3:$AJ$100,\\\"Inferred: residual\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\"Yes\\\")&\\\"/\\\"&SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$AI$3:$AI$100,\\\"<>\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\"Yes\\\")&\\\" inferred by residual\\\"\")\nlbl('  \\u2192 per-stage balance (Process 1)', 'R0/R1: 25 entrants \\u2212 16 inferred non-submitters (R020) \\u2212 2 low bidders (R022) = 7 continuing. R2: +1 (Party C, R024) \\u2212 2 non-submitters (R033\\u2013R034) \\u2212 4 dropped (R039\\u2013R042) = 2 continuing. R3: +2 re-entries (R044\\u2013R045) \\u2212 1 withdrawal (R049) \\u2212 2 signing outcomes (R055\\u2013R056) = 1 (winner). Total: 26 entrants + 2 re-entries \\u2212 27 exit units = 1. Balance formula below; Party A\\u2019s Count-0 identity row (R035) moves no counts.')\nlbl('  \\u2192 balance formula', \"=SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\\\"NDA signed\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\"Yes\\\")+SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\\\"Re-entered\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\"Yes\\\")-SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$AI$3:$AI$100,\\\"<>\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\"Yes\\\")\")\nhead('6. Comparability and inputs')\nlbl('Per-share basis', 'All offer prices are as-converted (preferred 100-for-1); the filing gives no decomposed values except G&W\\u2019s cash/CVR split. All amounts are US dollars; no currency conversion attempted.')\nlbl('Market benchmarks', 'Closing price 08/12/2016 (last trading day before announcement): $16.30 \\u2014 the $25.00 consideration is stated as a 53% premium (X-003). Closing price 09/16/2016: $24.88 (X-004). 2016 Q3 trading range through 09/16/2016: $15.60\\u2013$25.00 (X-005).')\nlbl('Share counts and optional calculation', '4,866,593 common + 640 preferred (as-converted 64,000) = 4,930,593 as-converted shares on the 09/16/2016 record date; 53,368 options (18,368 vested) and 43,500 RSUs held by directors/officers (X-006; X-005). Optional labelled calculation (not filing-stated, excludes options/RSUs): $25.00 \\u00d7 4,930,593 = $123.26 million implied equity value.')\nlbl('Contingent consideration', 'G&W\\u2019s July bids included a $1.13 per-share CVR tied to the subsequent sale of the South Quay property (book value $12.5 million used in BMO\\u2019s analyses); it is a contingent cash payment, so those bids remain All cash = Yes. The signed $25.00 terms exclude it.')\nlbl('Other-scope proposals', 'None disclosed: every indication, LOI and final bid is for 100% of the outstanding common stock on an as-converted basis (P-009). No segment, asset or minority-stake proposals; no separate Other-scope rows.')\nlbl('Valuation statements (not bids)', 'BMO\\u2019s implied per-share reference ranges: selected companies $10.95\\u2013$14.56 and $11.42\\u2013$15.09; precedent transactions $10.54\\u2013$26.50; DCF $10.82\\u2013$12.34 \\u2014 each compared with the $25.00 consideration (X-017\\u2013X-019). These are adviser analyses, not offers, and are not entered in bid-price cells.')\nlbl('Glossary', 'NDA = confidentiality agreement; IOI = indication of interest (non-binding); LOI = letter of intent (non-binding); CVR = contingent value right (extra cash tied to the South Quay property sale); confirmatory diligence = final-stage diligence after selection; data site = internet data room; exclusivity = target commitment to deal only with one bidder (requested by several bidders; never granted); go-shop = post-signing solicitation period (none); STB = Surface Transportation Board; as-converted = treating preferred as converted 100-for-1 into common. Layout-only HTML decoding and whitespace normalization were applied to the filing text in the Source text sheet.')\nlbl('Unverifiable items', 'Closing is not observed in this filing; the number of confidentiality agreements signed (25 vs 26) is reconciled in Q3; Party A\\u2019s later path is unresolved (Q5); no post-signing competition is disclosed.')\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Questions\nwsq = wb.create_sheet(QUESTIONS, 2)\nqhead = ['Q','Review topic','Recommended answer','Why and source','Affected rows/fields','Consequence of changing it','Status','Reviewer note']\nfor c, name in enumerate(qhead, 1):\n    cell = wsq.cell(row=1, column=c, value=name)\n    cell.font = hdr_font; cell.fill = hdr_fill; cell.alignment = Alignment(wrap_text=True, vertical='center')\nQ = [\n ('Q1', 'Process and round map, boundaries and finality',\n  'Keep one process and three rounds: R1 anchored on the week-of-03/28/2016 first outreach wave (R008), R2 opened mid-June 2016 by the LOI instruction (R023), R3 opened 07/27/2016 by selection and the move to definitive negotiation (R043). Round 0 keeps the pre-solicitation items with no Round opened row. Finality: R1 Not final; R2 and R3 Inferred final. Keep the 04/03\\u201304/06 convention meetings as one Information access changed row (R012) and Party C\\u2019s catch-up access as one row (R026); keep the 08/09\\u201308/11 G&W continued-diligence grant as a Material process update (R050). Post-signing: publicity row only (R057).',\n  'Preferred round-1 anchor is the executed outreach (P-004); rejected candidates R003 and R005 are retained as their own rows so the boundary can be moved. R2 alternative boundary 06/01/2016 (R021 advancement) rejected because no updated offers were sought then (P-008\\u2013P-009). R3 alternative boundaries 08/04 (prioritize Party B) and 08/12 (final bid/signing) rejected because definitive negotiation with the selected bidders demonstrably began on 07/27/2016 (P-020). R2 Inferred final because the target moved to confirmatory due diligence and definitive negotiation at its close; R3 Inferred final because it concluded with the executed agreement. Access rows follow section 4 (P-005; P-011).',\n  'R003, R005, R007, R008, R012, R021, R023, R026, R038, R043, R050, R057; Round, Round finality, What happened',\n  'Moving any boundary changes round-bidder tallies (9/6/3) and the round map in Summary; reclassifying the convention or catch-up access rows changes the access narrative but no counts.'),\n ('Q2', 'Deadline history and treatments',\n  'Record three versions: 05/10/2016 set by the 04/27/2016 board report (R016; superseded, no milestone row); revised to 05/19/2016 (R017; Extended) for the reason stated; 05/19/2016 reached while operative and treated Enforced (R018). The July 20, 2016 LOI due date (R023; R027) is treated Late bids accepted because G&W\\u2019s 07/21/2016 LOI and the other late-July LOIs were considered without a revision. G&W\\u2019s 6:00 p.m. 08/13/2016 offer expiry is not a bid deadline and stays in Terms (R052).',\n  'Deadline language and treatment rules are section 8.3. Receipt window 05/19\\u201306/01 straddles the due date, so no submission is late and Enforced (not Late bids accepted) applies (P-008). The revision reason is stated (P-007). The June LOI instruction carries its due date on the R2 opening row per section 8.3, with the milestone row at 07/20/2016 (P-009; P-012; P-014).',\n  'R016, R017, R018, R023 (Due date), R027, R052 (offer expiry in Terms); Deadline treatment, Due date, Date from/Date to of R017',\n  'Changing treatments alters the Summary deadline map and the R2 narrative; treating the May IOIs as late would contradict the filing\\u2019s receipt window.'),\n ('Q3', 'Confidentiality-agreement counts and auction screen',\n  'Working total: 26 executed confidentiality agreements \\u2014 the 25 of the week-of-03/28 wave (11 strategic + 14 financial) plus Party C\\u2019s early-July agreement (R009\\u2013R011, R024). Read the Board\\u2019s reasons\\u2019 \\u201c25 of whom entered into confidentiality agreements\\u201d as the reasons\\u2019 summary figure (X-002), which most likely omits Party C or treats one strategic signer differently; alternatively the wave could have produced 24 signatures (10 strategic + 14 financial) and the total 25 including Party C. Auction screen: met either way.',\n  'Background supplies both specific statements: \\u201cEach of the potential strategic buyers and 14 potential financial buyers subsequently executed confidentiality agreements\\u201d and Party C\\u2019s separate agreement after its early-July approach (P-004; P-011). The reasons cite 25 (X-002). Section 3.2 prefers the specific background passages; the conflict is preserved here rather than silently resolved.',\n  'R009, R010, R011, R024; Count cells; Summary \\u201cNDA signers\\u201d and auction screen',\n  'If the total is 25 including Party C, R009 drops to 9 strategic signers and the inferred residual (R020) stays 16 only if the submitter base is 9; otherwise the residual changes to 15 and the inferred share changes.'),\n ('Q4', 'Inferred closures and per-stage balance',\n  'Keep two inferred rows: R020 (Did not submit, Inferred: residual \\u2014 25 signers \\u2212 9 IOI submitters = 16, at the 05/19/2016 deadline) and R035 (Party A, Count 0, Inferred: identity, at 07/20/2016). All other outcomes are stated: two low bidders dropped 06/01 (R022), two LOI non-submitters (R033\\u2013R034), four 07/27 drops (R039\\u2013R042), one withdrawal (R049), two signing outcomes (R055\\u2013R056). Balance: R1 7 continuing; R2 2; R3 1 (winner); 16 of 27 exit units inferred.',\n  'Section 10.2 arithmetic; base from P-004 (25 signers) and P-008 (9 submitters). The base is a stated exact number, so no bounds are needed; if the Q3 count changes, the residual changes by the same amount (flag). R035 records only that Party A was out by the first named continuing set (P-012; P-020).',\n  'R020, R022, R033, R034, R035, R039\\u2013R042, R049, R055, R056; Count, Outcome basis, Decided by, Exit reason',\n  'Reclassifying any stated exit as inferred (or vice versa) changes the Summary inferred-share arithmetic and the per-stage balance table; moving R035 to 05/19/2016 would shift its transition but not any counts.'),\n ('Q5', 'Identity mappings, anonymous cohorts and non-participants',\n  'Recommended identities: the nine IOI submitters are Party B, G&W, Party D, Party E, Party F, the two unnamed low bidders and the two unnamed LOI non-submitters (one strategic, one financial). Party A is most likely the unnamed strategic LOI non-submitter (R033) and so is placed at 07/20/2016 with Count 0; alternatives are the 16 residual non-submitters (R020, which would move it to 05/19) or a low bidder (R022). Party B\\u2019s April 21, 2016 meeting and Party A\\u2019s March 22\\u201323 meetings are repeats within the 29-buyer wave (Count 0). GATX\\u2019s possible-buyer recusal is not a participation event; the two additional Class I railroads never entered.',\n  'Identifications follow the stage arithmetic (seven advancing = nine minus two low bidders; five of the seven plus Party C submitted LOIs) and the named LOI list (P-008; P-012; P-020). Party A\\u2019s last appearance is the memorandum recipient list (P-007). GATX: Director Smith recusal (P-020). Class I contacts: P-006.',\n  'R014, R015, R019, R022, R033, R034, R035; Who, Count, Related rows; Summary participant list',\n  'Re-identifying Party A (e.g., as a low bidder) would move its Count-0 row to R022 and change the reading of the two anonymous cohorts, but no counts are asserted on this basis either way.'),\n ('Q6', 'Formality, conditions and late reconfirmation calls',\n  'Formality: Formal for Party B (R028), G&W (R036\\u2013R037, R052) and Party D (R030, carried to R046) on returned agreement/voting-agreement mark-ups; Informal for the nine-IOI cohort (R019), Party C (R025, R031), Party E (R029, R047, R048) and Party F (R032) \\u2014 Party E\\u2019s issues summary is the borderline call (section 9.2 working default), flagged. Conditions: Heavy for the nine IOIs (pre-substantive-diligence context), C, D, E, F and G&W\\u2019s July LOIs (stated multi-week or exclusive diligence periods); Light for Party B (expedited review) and G&W\\u2019s 08/12 final bid (diligence completed; final documentation only; financing silent). No Bid reaffirmed row is recorded: Party B\\u2019s latest priced row is Formal and sits in an Inferred-final round, so the section 9.1 test fails; its August 4 revised draft gets no row (further draft in the definitive stage).',\n  'Formality signals and the issues-list default: P-013/P-016/P-014 mark-ups and P-015 (issues summary) via P-012. Conditions tests (Heavy triggers: stated multi-week or exclusive diligence; Heavy by context for pre-access indications): P-008, P-014\\u2013P-018, P-021, P-024. Late reconfirmation conditions (a)\\u2013(c): P-023, P-028; failure of condition (b).',\n  'R019, R025\\u2013R032, R035\\u2013R037, R046\\u2013R048, R052, R055 (Formality, Conditions level, Conditions detail, Terms or outcome)',\n  'Downgrading Party B or G&W to Informal changes the round\\u2019s documentation profile but not prices or counts; upgrading Party E to Formal would make it a formal LOI and would be noted in participants, without changing selection.'),\n ('Q7', 'Assigned Working dates that decide order',\n  'Conventions used (all disclosed in Date method): R008 03/28/2016 (first day of the outreach week, Assigned: bound); R009\\u2013R010 03/28/2016 (signing wave first day, Assigned: bound); R017 05/08/2016 (midpoint of the 04/27\\u201305/19 revision window); R019 05/19/2016 and R028\\u2013R032 07/20/2016 (solicitation due dates, Assigned: deadline); R039\\u2013R042 07/27/2016 (notifications after the decision, Assigned: decision day); R044\\u2013R045 07/29/2016. Within 08/12/2016 the order is G&W bid (morning) \\u2192 Board decision (afternoon) \\u2192 signing \\u2192 signing outcomes, per the stated sequence; the announcement follows on 08/15.',\n  'Section 8.1 rules 2\\u20136 and the order constraint; the May IOIs example (due date inside the receipt window) applies at R019. Same-day sequencing follows the filing\\u2019s own sequence (P-024; P-025; P-026; P-028).',\n  'Date from, Date to, Working date, Date basis, Date method of R008\\u2013R010, R017, R019, R028\\u2013R032, R039\\u2013R042, R044\\u2013R045, R052\\u2013R056',\n  'Changing an assigned date reorders rows (sorting is by Working date with # breaking ties) but not facts; the affected transitions are the annotation-heavy ones listed.'),\n ('Q8', 'Comparability, consideration form and normalization',\n  'Keep all per-share figures on the as-converted basis the filing used (P-008; P-009) and label the optional $123.26 million equity-value calculation as a non-filing arithmetic. Classify G&W\\u2019s July cash-plus-CVR bids as All cash = Yes (contingent cash, not securities) with the $1.13 South Quay CVR and payoff trigger in Terms. Record no Other-scope bids (all proposals were for 100% of the common on an as-converted basis). Keep BMO\\u2019s implied reference ranges in Summary only as valuation statements, never in bid-price cells.',\n  'Consideration rules (section 9.4): P-014 for the CVR split and South Quay basis; P-005/P-009/P-012 for note conversion basis; X-017\\u2013X-019 for the BMO ranges; X-005/X-006 for share counts. The $12.5 million South Quay book value is BMO\\u2019s input (X-005 range, P-026 text at page 38).',\n  'R019, R025\\u2013R032, R036\\u2013R037, R052, R054; Price kind/origin, Currency, All cash, Cash at closing; Summary comparability block',\n  'Treating the CVR as non-cash would change All cash to No for the July G&W bids; entering BMO\\u2019s ranges as prices would create false observations \\u2014 both are explicitly rejected above.'),\n]\nfor i, q in enumerate(Q, 2):\n    for c, v in enumerate(q, 1):\n        cell = wsq.cell(row=i, column=c, value=v)\n        cell.alignment = Alignment(wrap_text=True, vertical='top')\n        if c == 1: cell.font = Font(bold=True)\n    wsq.cell(row=i, column=7).value = 'Pending'\nfor col, w in zip('ABCDEFGH', [6, 34, 70, 70, 30, 42, 10, 18]):\n    wsq.column_dimensions[col].width = w\nwsq.freeze_panes = 'A2'\nwsq.auto_filter.ref = f'A1:H{len(Q)+1}'\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- final validations\nassert wb.sheetnames[:4] == [LEDGER, SUMMARY, QUESTIONS, SOURCE], wb.sheetnames\nassert wb[LISTS].sheet_state == 'hidden'\nos.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT), exist_ok=True)\nwb.save(OUT)\nprint('saved', OUT)\nprint('sheets:', wb.sheetnames)\nprint('source rows:', len(P_ROWS) + len(X_ROWS))\n"},"output":"Created file successfully: /tmp/opencode/build_workbook.py","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: /tmp/opencode/build_workbook.py"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/tmp/opencode/build_workbook.py\", \"content\": \"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Build providence-worcester.xlsx deal ledger from the PWRR DEFM14A (2016-09-20).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport re, json, bisect, os\\nfrom openpyxl import Workbook\\nfrom openpyxl.styles import Font, Alignment, PatternFill, Border, Side\\nfrom openpyxl.worksheet.datavalidation import DataValidation\\nfrom openpyxl.utils import get_column_letter\\n\\nTXT = '/tmp/opencode/pxw_text.txt'\\nOUT = '/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx'\\nlines = open(TXT, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\\\\n')\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- page map\\npm = json.load(open('/tmp/opencode/pagemap.json'))\\nmpos, mval = pm['mpos'], pm['mval']\\ndef page_for(i):\\n    j = bisect.bisect_left(mpos, i)\\n    return mval[j] if j < len(mval) else None\\n\\ndef clean(s):\\n    return re.sub(r'\\\\s+', ' ', s).strip()\\n\\nclass Source:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"A source text row with char->line mapping for page lookup.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    def __init__(self, sid, section, ranges):\\n        self.sid, self.section = sid, section\\n        chunks, lmap = [], []\\n        for (a, b) in ranges:              # 1-based inclusive\\n            for ln in range(a - 1, b):\\n                t = lines[ln]\\n                if not t.strip():\\n                    continue\\n                if chunks:\\n                    chunks.append(' ')\\n                    lmap.append(ln)\\n                chunks.append(t)\\n                lmap.extend([ln] * len(t))\\n        self.text = clean(''.join(chunks))\\n        # lmap currently indexes raw chunks incl. spaces; rebuild consistent:\\n        self.lmap = []\\n        self.text = ''\\n        for (a, b) in ranges:\\n            for ln in range(a - 1, b):\\n                t = clean(lines[ln])\\n                if not t:\\n                    continue\\n                if self.text:\\n                    self.text += ' '\\n                    self.lmap.append(ln)\\n                self.text += t\\n                self.lmap.extend([ln] * len(t))\\n        self.start_line = ranges[0][0] - 1\\n\\n    def page(self, offset=0):\\n        ln = self.lmap[min(offset, len(self.lmap) - 1)]\\n        return page_for(ln)\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- source rows\\nBG_SECTION = 'Proposal No. 1\\\\u2014The Merger \\\\u2014 Background of the Merger'\\nbg_segments = [\\n    (1161,1171),(1172,1184),(1185,1186),(1187,1193),(1194,1196),(1197,1201),\\n    (1202,1208),(1209,1213),(1214,1217),(1218,1220),(1221,1226),(1227,1229),\\n    (1230,1231),(1232,1235),(1238,1239),(1240,1241),(1242,1243),(1244,1245),\\n    (1246,1247),(1248,1255),(1256,1262),(1263,1271),(1272,1278),(1279,1285),\\n    (1286,1293),(1294,1303),(1304,1313),(1314,1316),(1317,1320),\\n]\\nP_ROWS = []\\nfor i, seg in enumerate(bg_segments, 1):\\n    P_ROWS.append(Source(f'P-{i:03d}', BG_SECTION, [seg]))\\n\\nX_DEFS = [\\n    ('X-001', 'Annex A \\\\u2014 Merger Agreement, Art. 1 (Definitions: Confidentiality Agreement)', [(4681,4682)]),\\n    ('X-002', 'Proposal No. 1\\\\u2014The Merger \\\\u2014 Recommendation of the Board of Directors and Reasons for the Merger', [(1338,1339)]),\\n    ('X-003', 'Proposal No. 1\\\\u2014The Merger \\\\u2014 Recommendation of the Board of Directors and Reasons for the Merger', [(1344,1348)]),\\n    ('X-004', 'Summary \\\\u2014 Market Price of Our Common Stock', [(667,670)]),\\n    ('X-005', 'Market Price of Common Stock', [(2739,2740)]),\\n    ('X-006', 'Summary \\\\u2014 Record Date; Outstanding Shares; Shares Entitled to Vote', [(377,381)]),\\n    ('X-007', 'Proposal No. 1\\\\u2014The Merger \\\\u2014 General', [(1154,1159)]),\\n    ('X-008', 'Summary \\\\u2014 Treatment of Equity and Equity-Based Awards', [(459,465)]),\\n    ('X-009', 'The Merger Agreement \\\\u2014 Regulatory Approvals Required for the Merger', [(2463,2469)]),\\n    ('X-010', 'The Merger Agreement \\\\u2014 Termination of the Merger Agreement (outside date)', [(556,559)]),\\n    ('X-011', 'The Merger Agreement \\\\u2014 Transaction Litigation', [(2470,2479)]),\\n    ('X-012', 'The Voting Agreement', [(2750,2752)]),\\n    ('X-013', 'Questions and Answers about the Merger and the Special Meeting', [(786,789)]),\\n    ('X-014', \\\"Proposal No. 1\\\\u2014The Merger \\\\u2014 Opinion of the Company's Financial Advisor\\\", [(1447,1452)]),\\n    ('X-015', 'Summary of Financial Analysis of BMO Capital Markets Corp. \\\\u2014 Miscellaneous (fees)', [(1672,1674)]),\\n    ('X-016', 'Summary of Financial Analysis of BMO Capital Markets Corp. \\\\u2014 Miscellaneous (relationships)', [(1679,1681)]),\\n    ('X-017', 'Summary of Financial Analysis of BMO Capital Markets Corp. \\\\u2014 Selected Publicly Traded Companies Analysis', [(1540,1545),(1582,1593)]),\\n    ('X-018', 'Summary of Financial Analysis of BMO Capital Markets Corp. \\\\u2014 Analysis of Selected Precedent Transactions', [(1597,1600),(1648,1653)]),\\n    ('X-019', 'Summary of Financial Analysis of BMO Capital Markets Corp. \\\\u2014 Discounted Cash Flow Analysis', [(1660,1668)]),\\n    ('X-020', 'The Parties to the Merger Agreement \\\\u2014 Providence and Worcester Railroad Company', [(966,976)]),\\n    ('X-021', 'The Parties to the Merger Agreement \\\\u2014 Genesee & Wyoming Inc.', [(978,985)]),\\n    ('X-022', 'Proposal No. 1\\\\u2014The Merger \\\\u2014 Recommendation of the Board of Directors and Reasons for the Merger (likelihood of completion)', [(1381,1384)]),\\n    ('X-023', 'Annex A \\\\u2014 Merger Agreement, Art. 1 (Definitions: Company Termination Fee)', [(4677,4677)]),\\n    ('X-024', 'Summary \\\\u2014 Voting Agreement', [(431,434)]),\\n]\\nX_ROWS = [Source(sid, sec, rngs) for sid, sec, rngs in X_DEFS]\\nSRC = {s.sid: s for s in P_ROWS + X_ROWS}\\n\\ndef quote(sid, start, end):\\n    s = SRC[sid]\\n    i = s.text.find(start)\\n    if i < 0:\\n        raise SystemExit(f'START not found in {sid}: {start[:60]}')\\n    j = s.text.find(end, i)\\n    if j < 0:\\n        raise SystemExit(f'END not found in {sid}: {end[:60]}')\\n    j += len(end)\\n    return s.text[i:j], s, i\\n\\ndef quotes(*specs):\\n    out, main, off = [], None, None\\n    for sid, a, b in specs:\\n        q, s, i = quote(sid, a, b)\\n        out.append(q)\\n        if main is None:\\n            main, off = s, i\\n    return out, main, off\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- ledger rows\\nCOLS = ['#','When','Who','What happened','Process','Round','Type','Terms or outcome',\\n        'Formality','Conditions level','Why and evidence','Source','Review','Reviewer note',\\n        'Row id','Include','Count','Date from','Date to','Working date','Date basis','Date method',\\n        'Price low','Price high','Price kind','Price origin','Currency','All cash','Cash at closing',\\n        'Conditions detail','Due date','Deadline treatment','Round finality','Decided by','Exit reason',\\n        'Outcome basis','Page','Related rows','Deal']\\nDEAL = 'PWRR-G&W 2016'\\n\\nUNKNOWN_NOTE = 'Type: Unknown \\\\u2014 unsplit population of mixed types (note, not Mixed).'\\n\\ndef R(when, who, what, rnd, typ, terms, why, src, review, count=None, df=None, dt=None,\\n      wa=None, basis=None, method=None, pl=None, ph=None, kind=None, origin=None, curr=None,\\n      cash=None, cclose=None, cdetail=None, due=None, dlm=None, rfin=None, dec=None, ex=None,\\n      ob=None, rel=None, price_note=False):\\n    return dict(when=when, who=who, what=what, rnd=rnd, typ=typ, terms=terms, why=why, src=src,\\n                review=review, count=count, df=df, dt=dt, wa=wa, basis=basis, method=method,\\n                pl=pl, ph=ph, kind=kind, origin=origin, curr=curr, cash=cash, cclose=cclose,\\n                cdetail=cdetail, due=due, dlm=dlm, rfin=rfin, dec=dec, ex=ex, ob=ob, rel=rel)\\n\\nrows = []\\ndef add(**kw):\\n    rows.append(R(**kw))\\n\\n# --- Round 0\\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-001', 'In the fourth quarter of 2015', 'enhance regional connectivity'))\\nadd(when='Q4 2015 (calendar quarter)', who='Party A (one of the Company\\\\u2019s Class I rail partners)',\\n    what='Bidder interest', rnd='0', typ='Strategic',\\n    terms='Unpriced approach: Party A suggested possible joint venture arrangements and expressed interest in acquiring equity in the Company to develop strategic opportunities and enhance regional connectivity; scope as to control not specified (not a whole-company bid); first sale-related contact, bidder-initiated, with the Chairman/CEO and the VP & Chief Commercial Officer; prompted the Board to form an investment-banker subcommittee. Count 1 = new first-contact party (a Bidder interest row carries the contact fact; see Summary contact tally).',\\n    why='Bidder interest (stated): the filing reports an unpriced expression of interest in acquiring equity, not a priced proposal; no per-share or value figures exist for it. Direction: bidder-to-target. Quote: \\\\u201c'+q+'\\\\u201d',\\n    src=['P-001'], review='Q5', count=1, df='2015-10-01', dt='2015-12-31', wa='2015-11-15',\\n    basis='Reported interval', method='Assigned: midpoint')\\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-001', 'the subcommittee recommended to the Board that the Company retain GHF', 'the Company engaged GHF'),\\n                   ('P-001', 'GHF represented to the Company that it would not represent any potential buyer', 'in connection with such an offer'))\\nadd(when='01/27/2016', who='GHF (Greene Holcomb & Fisher LLC) \\\\u2014 Company financial adviser; later BMO',\\n    what='Adviser engaged', rnd='0', typ=None,\\n    terms=\\\"Engaged as the Company's investment banking firm: subcommittee recommendation approved at the 01/27/2016 executive session (Director Smith absent); GHF presented qualifications and a proposed change-in-control process; represented it would not represent any potential buyer of the Company or any person proposing financing for such an offer; engagement followed the late-2015 banker interviews. GHF's business was acquired by BMO Capital Markets Corp. on 08/01/2016 \\\\u2014 the same adviser relationship continued as BMO (no second adviser row); aggregate fee ~$2.52 million.\\\",\\n    why='Adviser engaged (stated): engagement approval on the stated day; the engagement-letter date is not disclosed. The GHF-to-BMO acquisition is a firm change, not a new mandate (section 5.4). Quotes: \\\\u201c'+q[0]+'\\\\u201d / \\\\u201c'+q[1]+'\\\\u201d',\\n    src=['P-001','X-015'], review=None, df='2016-01-27', dt='2016-01-27', wa='2016-01-27',\\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported', rel='R003; mandate continued by BMO from 08/01/2016 (R052 source)')\\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-002', 'Representatives of GHF then proposed a process', 'regarding a change in control transaction'),\\n                   ('P-002', 'the Board appointed a special committee', 'a recommendation to the full Board'))\\nadd(when='03/14/2016', who='Board of Directors (special meeting)',\\n    what='Target sale decision', rnd='0', typ=None,\\n    terms='Decided to proceed with GHF\\\\u2019s proposed process: discussions with Party A plus solicitation of other third parties regarding a change in control transaction; qualified as an exploratory strategy, not a commitment to sell; appointed the Transaction Committee (Barrett (Chair), Anderson, Garvey) to supervise the process and recommend to the full Board; the Committee could not itself approve a change of control.',\\n    why='Target sale decision (stated): \\\\u201c'+q[0]+'\\\\u201d The qualification (exploratory strategy) is preserved. Committee appointment: \\\\u201c'+q[1]+'\\\\u201d',\\n    src=['P-002'], review='Q1', df='2016-03-14', dt='2016-03-14', wa='2016-03-14',\\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported', rel='candidate R1 anchor (rejected)')\\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-003', 'On March 22, 2016 and March 23, 2016', 'met with various representatives of Party A'),\\n                   ('P-004', 'met with various representatives of Party A on March 22 and 23, 2016', 'informed Party A of GHF\\\\u2019s engagement'))\\nadd(when='03/22/2016\\\\u201303/23/2016', who='Party A', what='Contact', rnd='0', typ='Strategic',\\n    terms='Management (CFO/Treasurer Noreck and other senior managers) met Party A representatives and informed Party A of GHF\\\\u2019s engagement. Repeat contact: Party A was already in contact from Q4 2015, so Count 0 (no double counting).',\\n    why='Contact (stated), repeat. Quotes: \\\\u201c'+q[0]+'\\\\u201d / \\\\u201c'+q[1]+'\\\\u201d Two-day series of meetings takes its first day as the Working date.',\\n    src=['P-003','P-004'], review=None, count=0, df='2016-03-22', dt='2016-03-23', wa='2016-03-22',\\n    basis='Reported interval', method='Assigned: bound')\\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-004', 'The Transaction Committee authorized GHF to contact Party A', 'change in control transaction'))\\nadd(when='03/24/2016', who='Transaction Committee', what='Target decision', rnd='0', typ=None,\\n    terms='Authorized GHF to contact Party A and other potential buyers to determine their interest in a change in control transaction. Candidate anchor for Round 1, rejected: an authorization to approach firms is not the completed outreach (the actual first wave is R007).',\\n    why='Target decision (stated): \\\\u201c'+q+'\\\\u201d Kept as a rejected R1 anchor row so the boundary can be moved.',\\n    src=['P-004'], review='Q1', df='2016-03-24', dt='2016-03-24', wa='2016-03-24',\\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported', rel='candidate R1 anchor (rejected); R008')\\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-004', 'representatives of each of GHF and the Company\\\\u2019s legal counsel', 'participated in all meetings of the Transaction Committee'))\\nadd(when='03/24/2016', who='Hinckley, Allen & Snyder LLP (Hinckley Allen) \\\\u2014 Company legal counsel',\\n    what='Adviser service observed', rnd='0', typ=None,\\n    terms='Company legal counsel; participated in all Transaction Committee meetings; engagement date not disclosed; first shown acting 03/24/2016.',\\n    why='Adviser service observed (stated): the filing shows Hinckley Allen already providing services on 03/24/2016; no selection or engagement date is disclosed, so the Working date is the earliest date shown acting. Quote: \\\\u201c'+q+'\\\\u201d',\\n    src=['P-004'], review=None, df='2016-03-24', dt='2016-03-24', wa='2016-03-24',\\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported')\\n# --- Round 1\\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-004', 'During the week of March 28, 2016', '18 potential financial buyers'))\\nadd(when='week of 03/28/2016', who='29 potential buyers (11 strategic incl. Party A; 18 financial)',\\n    what='Contact', rnd='1', typ='Unknown',\\n    terms='First outreach wave: GHF contacted 11 potential strategic buyers (including Party A) and 18 potential financial buyers in accordance with the Transaction Committee\\\\u2019s directives; Count 29 = disclosed cohort size (includes Party A, already in contact since Q4 2015). Type: Unknown \\\\u2014 cohort mixes strategic and financial (split supplied only for the signing wave, R009\\\\u2013R011).',\\n    why='Contact (stated cohort, executed outreach). Quote: \\\\u201c'+q+'\\\\u201d This is the R1 anchor event (see R008).',\\n    src=['P-004'], review='Q1', count=29, df='2016-03-28', dt='2016-04-03', wa='2016-03-28',\\n    basis='Reported interval', method='Assigned: bound', rel='R008 (anchor event)')\\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-004', 'During the week of March 28, 2016', '18 potential financial buyers'))\\nadd(when='week of 03/28/2016', who='Process (Round 1)', what='Round opened', rnd='1', typ=None,\\n    terms='R1 anchor: first outreach wave \\\\u2014 GHF contacted 11 potential strategic buyers (including Party A) and 18 potential financial buyers (R007); candidate anchors: R003 (03/14/2016 sale-strategy decision), R005 (03/24/2016 authorization to contact). Objective: solicit change-in-control interest and confirm continuing interest of NDA signers; the round runs through the IOI stage to the 06/01/2016 advancement decision. Round finality: Not final \\\\u2014 no final/binding/best-and-final announcement and no move to definitive negotiation; the stage closed by selection to management presentations (R021).',\\n    why='Round opened (convention/analytical). First outreach wave chosen under section 6.3(1); R003 and R005 are the retained rejected candidates. Quote: \\\\u201c'+q+'\\\\u201d',\\n    src=['P-004'], review='Q1', df='2016-03-28', dt='2016-04-03', wa='2016-03-28',\\n    basis='Reported interval', method='Assigned: bound', rfin='Not final', rel='anchor R007; candidates R003, R005')\\nqs, m, off = quotes(('P-004', 'Each of the potential strategic buyers', 'subsequently executed confidentiality agreements'),\\n                    ('P-004', 'did not contain any', 'acquire the Company'))\\nadd(when='from the week of 03/28/2016; by 04/22/2016', who='10 remaining potential strategic buyers (11 contacted less G&W)',\\n    what='NDA signed', rnd='1', typ='Strategic',\\n    terms='Confidentiality agreements signed by the potential strategic buyers of the outreach wave less G&W (recorded individually at R011); no \\\\u201cstandstill\\\\u201d or similar provision prohibiting a proposal or offer; the wave\\\\u2019s memorandum was distributed to signers including Party A, Party B and G&W.',\\n    why='NDA signed (stated cohort; residual after G&W\\\\u2019s individual row, section 5.2). Base: \\\\u201c'+qs[0]+'\\\\u201d / \\\\u201c'+qs[1]+'\\\\u201d Signing wave spans the reported period; Working date takes its first day. The memorandum distribution (R015 source) bounds the old-wave signings.',\\n    src=['P-004','P-007'], review='Q3', count=10, df='2016-03-28', dt='2016-04-22', wa='2016-03-28',\\n    basis='Relative only', method='Assigned: bound', rel='R011 (G&W); R010 (financial residual)')\\nadd(when='from the week of 03/28/2016; by 04/22/2016', who='14 potential financial buyers (of 18 contacted)',\\n    what='NDA signed', rnd='1', typ='Financial',\\n    terms='Confidentiality agreements signed by 14 of the 18 potential financial buyers contacted in the outreach wave; same no-standstill terms and memorandum distribution.',\\n    why='NDA signed (stated cohort). Quote: \\\\u201c'+qs[0]+'\\\\u201d / \\\\u201c'+qs[1]+'\\\\u201d',\\n    src=['P-004','P-007'], review='Q3', count=14, df='2016-03-28', dt='2016-04-22', wa='2016-03-28',\\n    basis='Relative only', method='Assigned: bound', rel='R009 (strategic residual)')\\nq1a, m, off = quotes(('X-001', 'shall mean the Confidentiality Agreement between the Company and Parent', 'April 3, 2016'))\\nq1b, m2, off2 = quotes(('P-007', 'including Party A, Party B and G&W', 'that had executed confidentiality agreements'))\\nadd(when='04/03/2016', who='G&W (Genesee & Wyoming Inc.)', what='NDA signed', rnd='1', typ='Strategic',\\n    terms='Acquisition-related confidentiality agreement between the Company and G&W dated 04/03/2016 (the merger agreement\\\\u2019s defined \\\\u201cConfidentiality Agreement\\\\u201d); G&W also met management at the 2016 Connections Convention (04/03\\\\u201304/06) and received the memorandum.',\\n    why='NDA signed (stated): the merger agreement definition fixes G&W\\\\u2019s individual date; the wave cohort rows (R009\\\\u2013R010) exclude it. Quotes: \\\\u201c'+q1a+'\\\\u201d / \\\\u201c'+q1b+'\\\\u201d',\\n    src=['X-001','P-012'], review='Q3', count=1, df='2016-04-03', dt='2016-04-03', wa='2016-04-03',\\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported', rel='R009/R010 (wave cohorts)')\\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-005', 'held a series of introductory meetings with five potential strategic buyers', '2016 Connections Convention'))\\nadd(when='04/03/2016\\\\u201304/06/2016', who='Five unnamed potential strategic buyers (incl. G&W)',\\n    what='Information access changed', rnd='1', typ='Strategic',\\n    terms='GHF and Company management held a series of introductory management meetings with five potential strategic buyers (incl. G&W) at the American Short Line and Regional Railroad Association\\\\u2019s 2016 Connections Convention; the 14 financial-signer bidders and other NDA signers received no comparable management meetings at that time; venue-based opportunity (no selection reason stated for the five). Count blank (access row).',\\n    why='Information access changed (classification): management meetings given to some live bidders and not others, recorded once for the access decision (not per meeting). Quote: \\\\u201c'+q+'\\\\u201d',\\n    src=['P-005'], review='Q1', df='2016-04-03', dt='2016-04-06', wa='2016-04-03',\\n    basis='Reported interval', method='Assigned: bound')\\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-006', 'the Transaction Committee authorized representatives of GHF, on behalf of', 'to confirm their continuing interest'))\\nadd(when='04/07/2016', who='Transaction Committee', what='Target decision', rnd='1', typ=None,\\n    terms='Authorized GHF to contact the five convention parties, other potential strategic buyers (including certain Class I railroads) and private equity firms under NDA to confirm their continuing interest.',\\n    why='Target decision (stated). Quote: \\\\u201c'+q+'\\\\u201d',\\n    src=['P-006'], review=None, df='2016-04-07', dt='2016-04-07', wa='2016-04-07',\\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported')\\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-006', 'Mr. Noreck reported', 'in a possible transaction'))\\nadd(when='by 04/07/2016; day not disclosed', who='Two unnamed additional Class I railroads',\\n    what='Contact', rnd='1', typ='Strategic',\\n    terms='Approached by the Company (management) before the 04/07/2016 committee report to gauge interest in a possible transaction; no NDA, bid or further participation reported; they never entered the process (no outcome row). Count 2 = cohort size.',\\n    why='Contact (stated): \\\\u201c'+q+'\\\\u201d Direction: target-to-bidder; approach precedes the 04/07/2016 meeting (day not disclosed), so the lower bound is the report date.',\\n    src=['P-006'], review=None, count=2, df=None, dt='2016-04-07', wa='2016-04-07',\\n    basis='Relative only', method='Assigned: bound')\\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-006', 'Subsequently, on April 21, 2016', 'another potential strategic buyer'))\\nadd(when='04/21/2016', who='Party B', what='Contact', rnd='1', typ='Strategic',\\n    terms='Introductory meeting held by the Company and GHF with Party B; first individually recorded meeting for Party B. Repeat contact: Party B is treated as one of the contacted NDA signers of the March wave (R007/R009), so Count 0; the alternative reading is flagged in Q5.',\\n    why='Contact (stated), repeat within the wave. Quote: \\\\u201c'+q+'\\\\u201d',\\n    src=['P-006'], review='Q5', count=0, df='2016-04-21', dt='2016-04-21', wa='2016-04-21',\\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported')\\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-007', 'each potential buyer had been advised', 'May 10, 2016'))\\nadd(when='by 04/27/2016; IOI deadline 05/10/2016', who='Process (all potential buyers)',\\n    what='Deadline set', rnd='1', typ=None,\\n    terms='Each potential buyer advised to submit a non-binding indication of interest by 05/10/2016; advice reported at the 04/27/2016 executive session of the Board; deadline version 1 (later revised, R017). Communicating day not disclosed.',\\n    why='Deadline set (stated); known only by the 04/27/2016 report. Quote: \\\\u201c'+q+'\\\\u201d This date was superseded before arrival, so it stays in the set/revised history without a milestone row.',\\n    src=['P-007'], review='Q2', due='2016-05-10', df=None, dt='2016-04-27', wa='2016-04-27',\\n    basis='Relative only', method='Assigned: bound')\\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-007', 'which deadline was subsequently postponed to May 19, 2016', 'most compelling offers'))\\nadd(when='after 04/27/2016; day not disclosed (new deadline 05/19/2016)', who='Process (all potential buyers)',\\n    what='Deadline revised', rnd='1', typ=None,\\n    terms='IOI deadline postponed from 05/10/2016 to 05/19/2016 to ensure potential buyers had sufficient time to formulate their most compelling offers; requester not disclosed; all potential buyers affected. Treatment: Extended \\\\u2014 this row moved the 05/10/2016 due date (recorded here and in the Summary map).',\\n    why='Deadline revised (stated). Quote: \\\\u201c'+q+'\\\\u201d Revision day not disclosed; window 04/27\\\\u201305/19 bounded by the 04/27 report and the new due date; midpoint assigned.',\\n    src=['P-007'], review='Q2', due='2016-05-19', dlm='Extended', df='2016-04-27', dt='2016-05-19',\\n    wa='2016-05-08', basis='Relative only', method='Assigned: midpoint', rel='moves R016 (05/10) to 05/19')\\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-008', 'Between May 19, 2016 and June 1, 2016', 'nine written indications of interest'),\\n                   ('P-008', 'the Transaction Committee concluded that the two low bidders should be excluded', 'remaining seven potential buyers'))\\nadd(when='05/19/2016', who='Process (all potential buyers)', what='Deadline', rnd='1', typ=None,\\n    terms='IOI deadline reached while operative; nine IOIs were received between 05/19 and 06/01 (a window that straddles the due date, so no submission is treated as late) and the committee took its next step on the bids in hand (05/23 and 06/01 reviews; exclusions and advancement). Treatment: Enforced.',\\n    why='Deadline (stated milestone; treatment convention). Quotes: \\\\u201c'+q[0]+'\\\\u201d / \\\\u201c'+q[1]+'\\\\u201d',\\n    src=['P-008'], review='Q2', due='2016-05-19', dlm='Enforced', df='2016-05-19', dt='2016-05-19',\\n    wa='2016-05-19', basis='Reported day', method='Reported')\\nq, m, off = quotes(('P-008', 'Between May 19, 2016 and June 1, 2016', 'equity values of $90 million to $134 million'))\\nadd(when='05/19/2016\\\\u201306/01/2016', who='Nine IOI submitters (anonymous cohort)', what='Bid', rnd='1',\\n    typ='Unknown',\\n    terms='Nine written non-binding indications of interest at $17.93\\\\u2013$26.50 per share (as-converted; group envelope across the cohort, not any member\\\\u2019s price), implying equity values of $90\\\\u2013134 million; made before substantive d