016-08-02', dt='2016-08-02', wa='2016-08-02',\\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported', dec='Bidder', ex='Terms or process', ob='Stated',\\n    rel='after revised LOI R046; dropped R040; re-entered R044')\\nq = quotes(('P-023', 'G&W requested that it be allowed to continue its due diligence', 'which request was granted'),\\n           ('P-023', 'On August 11, 2016, G&W indicated', 'physical diligence of the Company'))\\nadd('08/09/2016\\\\u201308/11/2016', 'G&W', 'Material process update', '3', 'Strategic',\\n    'Continued due diligence granted to G&W: after the 08/09/2016 decision directing BMO to tell G&W that the Company intended to enter a merger agreement with another bidder, G&W requested continued due diligence to potentially facilitate an improved offer; the request was granted and G&W completed physical diligence on 08/10\\\\u201308/11/2016, then indicated a possible revised LOI for 08/12/2016. Precise action: access/continued diligence granted to a rival after the target\\\\u2019s selection of Party B.',\\n    'Material process update (stated): consequential development with no more specific label; it preceded G&W\\\\u2019s 08/12/2016 bid. Quotes: \\\\u201c' + q[0] + '\\\\u201d / \\\\u201c' + q[1] + '\\\\u201d',\\n    ['P-023'], 'Q1', df='2016-08-09', dt='2016-08-11', wa='2016-08-09',\\n    basis='Reported interval', method='Assigned: bound')\\nq = quotes(('P-023', 'representatives of Hinckley Allen and Simpson', 'legal counsel'))\\nadd('08/10/2016', 'Simpson Thacher & Bartlett LLP (Simpson Thacher) \\\\u2014 G&W legal counsel',\\n    'Adviser service observed', '3', None,\\n    'G&W\\\\u2019s legal counsel; first shown acting 08/10/2016 (discussed merger agreement and voting agreement provisions with Hinckley Allen and received a revised disclosure letter); engagement date not disclosed.',\\n    'Adviser service observed (stated): the filing shows Simpson Thacher acting; no engagement date. Quote: \\\\u201c' + q[0] + '\\\\u201d',\\n    ['P-023'], None, df='2016-08-10', dt='2016-08-10', wa='2016-08-10',\\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported')\\nq = quotes(('P-024', 'G&W submitted a revised LOI to acquire the Company', 'on the following'))\\nadd('08/12/2016 (morning)', 'G&W', 'Bid', '3', 'Strategic',\\n    'Revised LOI at $25.00 per share in cash (as-converted; point), dropping the previously proposed CVR, together with mark-ups of the merger agreement and voting agreement; offer stated to expire 6:00 p.m. on 08/13/2016; submitted after G&W completed physical diligence and after the Company told G&W it intended to sign with another bidder; first G&W bid in Round 3 (Count 1).',\\n    'Bid (stated final price revision). Quote: \\\\u201c' + q[0] + '\\\\u201d Formality: returned agreement and voting-agreement markups plus a price confirmation in definitive negotiation \\\\u2192 Formal. Conditions: diligence completed 08/11/2016, no diligence or exclusivity condition attached, no Heavy trigger reported \\\\u2192 Light (financing silent; silence does not raise or lower the level, and None is not claimed because financing is not stated). All cash: Yes; cash at closing $25.00.',\\n    ['P-024'], 'Q6; Q8', count=1, df='2016-08-12', dt='2016-08-12', wa='2016-08-12',\\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported', formality='Formal', cond='Light',\\n    pl=25.00, ph=25.00, kind='Point', origin='Stated', curr='USD', cash='Yes', cclose=25.00,\\n    cdetail='Fin: not stated; DD required: none; DD open: no; Excl: none', rel='revises R037')\\nq = quotes(('P-026', 'representatives of BMO then contacted Party B', 'would not increase its price'),\\n           ('P-027', 'The Board determined that the G&W offer represented the superior proposal', 'superior proposal'),\\n           ('P-027', 'Following a discussion of the terms of the merger agreement', 'plan of merger'))\\nadd('08/12/2016 (afternoon; Transaction Committee met 10:30 a.m.)',\\n    'Board of Directors (special meeting; Director Smith recused)', 'Target decision', '3', None,\\n    'After the Committee\\\\u2019s 10:30 a.m. meeting (BMO directed to inform Party B that a higher revised LOI had been received) and the Board\\\\u2019s comparison of the two drafts (G&W $1.00 per share higher; lower termination fee; STB approval timing not materially different; no financing condition), the Board asked BMO to seek a higher price from Party B \\\\u2014 Party B declined; the Board determined G&W\\\\u2019s offer a superior proposal, received BMO\\\\u2019s oral fairness opinion (written opinion dated 08/12/2016, to holders other than the Eder Trusts) and approved the merger agreement and recommended shareholder approval.',\\n    'Target decision (stated). Quotes: \\\\u201c' + q[0] + '\\\\u201d / \\\\u201c' + q[1] + '\\\\u201d / \\\\u201c' + q[2] + '\\\\u201d',\\n    ['P-026', 'P-027', 'P-029'], 'Q6', df='2016-08-12', dt='2016-08-12', wa='2016-08-12',\\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported', rel='bid R052; signing R054; outcomes R055\\\\u2013R056')\\nq = quotes(('P-028', 'the Company and G&W executed the merger agreement', 'executed the voting agreement'),\\n           ('X-023', 'shall mean $3,785,000', '$3,785,000'))\\nadd('08/12/2016', 'PWRR, G&W and Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc.', 'Merger agreement signed', '3', None,\\n    'Executed the merger agreement (Merger Sub merges into PWRR, which survives as a wholly owned G&W subsidiary; $25.00 cash per common share; preferred converted 100-for-1 plus accrued dividends; equity awards cashed out) and, with the Eder Trusts, the voting agreement (842,742 common / 500 preferred; ~17.3% / 78.1% of record-date class shares). Company termination fee $3,785,000 (~3% of transaction value; G&W draft negotiated down from 3.85%; Party B\\\\u2019s draft was 3% plus expenses capped at 1%); no financing condition; outside dates 12/31/2016, or 02/28/2017 if only STB approval remains. Signing is not a bid row: agreed consideration stated here, price/formality/conditionality cells left blank.',\\n    'Merger agreement signed (stated). Quotes: \\\\u201c' + q[0] + '\\\\u201d / \\\\u201c' + q[1] + '\\\\u201d Termination-fee and fiduciary-out terms were consequential for selection and are folded into this row (section 4).',\\n    ['P-028', 'X-023', 'X-010', 'P-026'], 'Q8', df='2016-08-12', dt='2016-08-12', wa='2016-08-12',\\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported', rel='Board approval R053')\\nq = quotes(('P-026', 'representatives of BMO then contacted Party B', 'would not increase its price'))\\nadd('by 08/12/2016', 'Party B', 'Not selected at signing', '3', 'Strategic',\\n    'Still bidding when the target chose another: standing $24.00 LOI; asked to improve and declined; the target signed with G&W. Decided by: Target; Exit reason: Would not improve earlier offer. Outcome basis: Stated (the target chose another while Party B remained live).',\\n    'Not selected at signing (stated). Quote: \\\\u201c' + q[0] + '\\\\u201d A bidder asked to improve and declining takes Would not improve earlier offer even though the target then chose the rival and Decided by is Target (section 10.3). No late-reconfirmation row is recorded for Party B: its latest priced row (R028) is Formal and sits in a round whose finality is Inferred final, so the section 9.1 test is not met.',\\n    ['P-026', 'P-028'], 'Q6', count=1, df=None, dt='2016-08-12', wa='2016-08-12',\\n    basis='Relative only', method='Assigned: bound', dec='Target', ex='Would not improve earlier offer',\\n    ob='Stated', rel='standing bid R028; signing R054')\\nq = quotes(('P-021', 'confirmed its original proposal of $21.26 per share', '$21.26 per share'),\\n           ('P-027', 'The Board determined that the G&W offer represented the superior proposal', 'superior proposal'))\\nadd('by 08/12/2016', 'Party E', 'Not selected at signing', '3', 'Strategic',\\n    'Still live when the target chose another: standing original proposal of $21.26 per share confirmed 08/02/2016; not chosen against G&W\\\\u2019s $25.00. Decided by: Target; Exit reason: Lower offer than rivals.',\\n    'Not selected at signing (stated). Quotes: \\\\u201c' + q[0] + '\\\\u201d / \\\\u201c' + q[1] + '\\\\u201d Party E was not displaced by exclusivity (none was executed), so this is a signing outcome, not an earlier withdrawal.',\\n    ['P-021', 'P-027', 'P-028'], 'Q4', count=1, df=None, dt='2016-08-12', wa='2016-08-12',\\n    basis='Relative only', method='Assigned: bound', dec='Target', ex='Lower offer than rivals',\\n    ob='Stated', rel='standing bid R048')\\nq = quotes(('P-028', 'The Company issued a press release publicly announcing the transaction on Monday, August 15, 2016', 'opening of trading of'))\\nadd('08/15/2016', 'PWRR (press release)', 'Merger announced', 'post', None,\\n    'Company press release publicly announcing the transaction on Monday, 08/15/2016 before the opening of NASDAQ trading; issuer: the Company; medium: press release. No go-shop, competing post-signing proposal, agreement termination or closing is disclosed in this filing.',\\n    'Merger announced (stated publicity). Quote: \\\\u201c' + q[0] + '\\\\u201d',\\n    ['P-028'], 'Q1', df='2016-08-15', dt='2016-08-15', wa='2016-08-15',\\n    basis='Reported day', method='Reported')\\n\\n# sanity: working dates never decrease\\nprev = None\\nfor i, r in enumerate(rows, 1):\\n    assert r['wa'] >= (prev or ''), (i, r['wa'], prev)\\n    prev = r['wa']\\nNROWS = len(rows)\\nprint('ledger rows:', NROWS)\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- workbook\\nwb = Workbook()\\nLEDGER, SUMMARY, QUESTIONS, SOURCE, LISTS = 'Deal ledger', 'Summary', 'Questions', 'Source text', 'Lists'\\nws = wb.active; ws.title = LEDGER\\nCOLS = ['#','When','Who','What happened','Process','Round','Type','Terms or outcome','Formality',\\n        'Conditions level','Why and evidence','Source','Review','Reviewer note','Row id','Include','Count',\\n        'Date from','Date to','Working date','Date basis','Date method','Price low','Price high','Price kind',\\n        'Price origin','Currency','All cash','Cash at closing','Conditions detail','Due date',\\n        'Deadline treatment','Round finality','Decided by','Exit reason','Outcome basis','Page','Related rows','Deal']\\nhdr_fill = PatternFill('solid', fgColor='1F3864')\\nhdr_font = Font(bold=True, color='FFFFFF', size=10)\\ngrp = {15:'Row identity', 17:'Count', 18:'Dates', 23:'Price', 28:'Settlement', 30:'Conditions detail',\\n       31:'Deadline & finality', 34:'Outcome', 37:'Source page', 38:'Related rows', 39:'Deal'}\\ngrp_fill = PatternFill('solid', fgColor='D9E1F2')\\nfor c, name in enumerate(COLS, 1):\\n    cell = ws.cell(row=2, column=c, value=name)\\n    cell.font = hdr_font; cell.fill = hdr_fill\\n    cell.alignment = Alignment(wrap_text=True, vertical='center')\\n    if c in grp:\\n        g = ws.cell(row=1, column=c, value=grp[c])\\n        g.font = Font(bold=True, size=9, color='1F3864'); g.fill = grp_fill\\n        g.alignment = Alignment(vertical='center')\\n\\nfor i, r in enumerate(rows):\\n    rr = 3 + i\\n    main = r['src'][0]\\n    label = '; '.join(r['src']) + ' (main: ' + main + ')'\\n    vals = [i + 1, r['when'], r['who'], r['what'], 1, r['rnd'], r['typ'], r['terms'],\\n            r['formality'], r['cond'], r['why'],\\n            f'=HYPERLINK(\\\"#{SOURCE}!$D${SRC_ROW[main]}\\\",\\\"{label}\\\")',\\n            r['review'], None, f'R{i+1:03d}', 'Yes', r['count'], r['df'], r['dt'], r['wa'],\\n            r['basis'], r['method'], r['pl'], r['ph'], r['kind'], r['origin'], r['curr'],\\n            r['cash'], r['cclose'], r['cdetail'], r['due'], r['dlm'], r['rfin'], r['dec'],\\n            r['ex'], r['ob'], r['page'], r['rel'], DEAL]\\n    for c, v in enumerate(vals, 1):\\n        ws.cell(row=rr, column=c, value=v)\\nqrow = 2 + NROWS\\nwide = {2:20,3:32,4:19,5:8,6:7,7:11,8:72,9:11,10:12,11:95,12:34,13:9,14:14}\\nfor c, w in wide.items():\\n    ws.column_dimensions[get_column_letter(c)].width = w\\nfor c in range(15, 40):\\n    ws.column_dimensions[get_column_letter(c)].width = 14\\nfor c in range(1, 40):\\n    for rr in range(3, qrow + 1):\\n        ws.cell(row=rr, column=c).alignment = Alignment(\\n            wrap_text=(c in (2,3,4,8,11,12,14) or c >= 15), vertical='top')\\nfor rr in range(3, qrow + 1):\\n    for c in (18,19,20,31):\\n        ws.cell(row=rr, column=c).number_format = 'mm/dd/yyyy'\\n    for c in (23,24,29):\\n        ws.cell(row=rr, column=c).number_format = '0.00'\\n    ws.cell(row=rr, column=12).font = Font(color='0563C1', underline='single', size=9)\\nws.freeze_panes = 'D3'\\nws.auto_filter.ref = f'A2:AM{qrow}'\\nfor c in range(15, 40):\\n    cd = ws.column_dimensions[get_column_letter(c)]\\n    cd.outlineLevel = 1; cd.hidden = True\\nws.sheet_properties.outlinePr.summaryRight = True\\n\\n# source sheet\\nwss = wb.create_sheet(SOURCE)\\nfor c, name in enumerate(['Paragraph','Section','Page','Text'], 1):\\n    cell = wss.cell(row=1, column=c, value=name)\\n    cell.font = hdr_font; cell.fill = hdr_fill\\n    cell.alignment = Alignment(wrap_text=True, vertical='center')\\nfor i, s in enumerate(P_ROWS + X_ROWS):\\n    rr = i + 2\\n    wss.cell(row=rr, column=1, value=s.sid)\\n    wss.cell(row=rr, column=2, value=s.section)\\n    wss.cell(row=rr, column=3, value=s.page(0))\\n    wss.cell(row=rr, column=4, value=s.text)\\n    wss.cell(row=rr, column=4).alignment = Alignment(wrap_text=True, vertical='top')\\n    wss.cell(row=rr, column=2).alignment = Alignment(wrap_text=True, vertical='top')\\nwss.column_dimensions['A'].width = 11\\nwss.column_dimensions['B'].width = 46\\nwss.column_dimensions['C'].width = 8\\nwss.column_dimensions['D'].width = 150\\nwss.freeze_panes = 'A2'\\nwss.auto_filter.ref = f'A1:D{len(P_ROWS)+len(X_ROWS)+1}'\\n\\n# Lists + validations\\nwsl = wb.create_sheet(LISTS)\\nLISTS_DEF = {\\n 'What happened': ['Target interest','Bidder interest','Target sale decision','Activist pressure','Activist involvement',\\n   'Adviser engaged','Adviser service observed','Adviser ended','Contact','NDA signed','Round opened','Deadline set',\\n   'Deadline revised','Deadline','Target decision','Information access changed','Material process update',\\n   'Exclusivity changed','Bid','Bid reaffirmed','Offer update','Other-scope bid','Valuation statement',\\n   'Bidding group changed','Joined group','Dropped by target','Withdrew','Did not submit','Participation paused',\\n   'Re-entered','Not selected at signing','Sale process announced','Bid announced','Merger announced',\\n   'Merger agreement signed','Go-shop changed','Process terminated','Process restarted','Agreement terminated','Closed'],\\n 'Type': ['Strategic','Financial','Mixed','Unknown'],\\n 'Formality': ['Formal','Informal','Insufficient evidence','Varies'],\\n 'Conditions level': ['None','Light','Heavy','Insufficient evidence','Varies'],\\n 'Include': ['Yes','No'],\\n 'Date basis': ['Reported day','Inferred day','Reported interval','Approximate window','Relative only','Undated'],\\n 'Date method': ['Reported','Inferred','Assigned: deadline','Assigned: decision day','Assigned: midpoint','Assigned: bound','Assigned: sequence'],\\n 'Price kind': ['Point','Bidder range','Group envelope','Bound only','Undisclosed'],\\n 'Price origin': ['Stated','Carried forward','Inferred'],\\n 'All cash': ['Yes','No','Not stated'],\\n 'Deadline treatment': ['Extended','Extended; Late bids accepted','Late bids accepted','Enforced','Passed without action','Unclear','No deadline stated'],\\n 'Round finality': ['Announced as final','Inferred final','Not final'],\\n 'Decided by': ['Bidder','Target','Both','Unknown'],\\n 'Exit reason': ['Value below market price','Value at or below market price','Value below earlier offer','Value at earlier offer',\\n   'Would not improve earlier offer','Lower offer than rivals','Terms or process','Other stated reason','Not stated'],\\n 'Outcome basis': ['Stated','Inferred: residual','Inferred: exclusivity','Inferred: silent','Inferred: identity'],\\n}\\nlist_ranges = {}\\nfor li, (name, vals) in enumerate(LISTS_DEF.items(), 1):\\n    col = get_column_letter(li)\\n    c = wsl.cell(row=1, column=li, value=name); c.font = Font(bold=True)\\n    for j, v in enumerate(vals, 2):\\n        wsl.cell(row=j, column=li, value=v)\\n    list_ranges[name] = f\\\"'{LISTS}'!${col}$2:${col}${len(vals)+1}\\\"\\nwsl.sheet_state = 'hidden'\\ndv_map = {'What happened': 4, 'Type': 7, 'Formality': 9, 'Conditions level': 10, 'Include': 16,\\n          'Date basis': 21, 'Date method': 22, 'Price kind': 25, 'Price origin': 26, 'All cash': 28,\\n          'Deadline treatment': 32, 'Round finality': 33, 'Decided by': 34, 'Exit reason': 35,\\n          'Outcome basis': 36}\\nfor name, col in dv_map.items():\\n    dv = DataValidation(type='list', formula1=list_ranges[name], allow_blank=True,\\n                        showErrorMessage=True, errorStyle='warning')\\n    ws.add_data_validation(dv)\\n    L = get_column_letter(col)\\n    dv.add(f'{L}3:{L}{qrow}')\\n\\n# Summary\\nwsu = wb.create_sheet(SUMMARY, 1)\\nwsu.column_dimensions['A'].width = 36\\nwsu.column_dimensions['B'].width = 155\\nrow = [1]\\ndef head(text):\\n    c = wsu.cell(row=row[0], column=1, value=text); c.font = Font(bold=True, size=12, color='1F3864')\\n    row[0] += 1\\ndef lbl(text, val=''):\\n    a = wsu.cell(row=row[0], column=1, value=text); a.font = Font(bold=True, size=10)\\n    a.alignment = Alignment(wrap_text=True, vertical='top')\\n    b = wsu.cell(row=row[0], column=2, value=val); b.alignment = Alignment(wrap_text=True, vertical='top')\\n    row[0] += 1\\nt = wsu.cell(row=row[0], column=1, value='PWRR \\\\u00d7 G&W \\\\u2014 deal ledger summary (Providence and Worcester Railroad Company / Genesee & Wyoming Inc., 2016)')\\nt.font = Font(bold=True, size=13); row[0] += 1\\nhead('1. Status and commercial account')\\nlbl('Delivery status', 'AI first pass; not human-approved. Instruction: SEC_Deal_Ledger_Extraction_Instruction.md, revision of 19 September 2026 (short form). Supplied source: providence-worcester_2016-09-20_DEFM14A.htm \\\\u2014 PWRR definitive proxy statement (DEFM14A) filed 09/20/2016, proxy dated 09/19/2016. Source coverage: the complete \\\\u201cBackground of the Merger\\\\u201d (pp. 27\\\\u201332) is reproduced in order in the Source text sheet (P-001\\\\u2013P-029), with every other passage used as X-001 onward.')\\nlbl('Commercial account', 'Initiation was mixed: a Q4 2015 approach by a Class I rail partner (Party A) expressing interest in acquiring equity led, through the Board\\\\u2019s banker search and its 03/14/2016 decision to explore a change of control, to a broad bank-run solicitation of 29 potential buyers (11 strategic, 18 financial) in the week of 03/28/2016. '\\n    'Twenty-five buyers signed confidentiality agreements (no standstills); after introductory meetings and a memorandum, nine submitted non-binding IOIs received 05/19\\\\u201306/01/2016 at $17.93\\\\u2013$26.50 per share as-converted (equity values $90\\\\u2013134 million), and the committee excluded the two lowest and advanced seven to management presentations and a data site. '\\n    'A mid-June solicitation for LOIs with agreement mark-ups (due 07/20/2016) produced six LOIs in late July at $19.20\\\\u2013$24.00: Party B ($24.00) and G&W ($21.15, then $22.15 including a $1.13 South Quay CVR) led; Party E ($21.26), Party D ($21.00), Party C ($19.30) and Party F ($19.20) followed; one strategic and one financial buyer elected not to submit. '\\n    'On 07/27/2016 the committee chose G&W and Party B for confirmatory due diligence and definitive negotiation and told the remaining bidders they were out; Party D and Party E briefly re-engaged (08/01 revised LOIs of $24.00 and $23.81, Party E supported by Party F financing), but Party D withdrew on 08/02 after the Company declined a no-sign commitment and Party E reverted to $21.26. '\\n    'On 08/12/2016 G&W\\\\u2019s final $25.00 all-cash LOI (CVR dropped, mark-ups returned, expiry 6:00 p.m. 08/13) displaced Party B\\\\u2019s $24.00 after Party B declined to raise, and the Board approved the merger agreement and the Eder Trusts\\\\u2019 voting agreement that same day. '\\n    'Announcement followed on 08/15/2016; no go-shop, competing post-signing proposal, agreement termination or closing is disclosed, STB approval was pending (petition 09/01/2016; voting trust submission 09/14/2016), and closing was expected in Q4 2016.')\\nhead('2. Deal facts')\\nlbl('Target', 'Providence and Worcester Railroad Company (PWRR), a Rhode Island corporation; regional freight railroad in Massachusetts, Rhode Island, Connecticut and New York; NASDAQ: PWX; US public company. 4,866,593 common shares and 640 preferred shares outstanding on the 09/16/2016 record date (preferred convertible 100-for-1; non-cumulative $5.00 dividend).')\\nlbl('Focal acquirer and type', 'Genesee & Wyoming Inc. (G&W), a Delaware corporation; NYSE: GWR; US public company; Strategic \\\\u2014 operating short-line/regional railroad acquirer, buying through its wholly owned shell Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc. (formed 08/12/2016).')\\nlbl('Agreed consideration', '$25.00 per share in cash (as-converted basis: preferred deemed converted into 100 common shares plus accrued and unpaid dividends); equity awards cashed out at $25.00 (options net of exercise price; RSUs at $25.00); no financing condition; G&W representation as to financial wherewithal. All cash: Yes. No CVR in the signed terms.')\\nlbl('Signing', '08/12/2016 \\\\u2014 merger agreement among PWRR, G&W and Merger Sub; voting agreement among PWRR, G&W and the Eder Trusts (842,742 common shares, 500 preferred shares).')\\nlbl('Announcement', '08/15/2016 \\\\u2014 Company press release before the opening of NASDAQ trading.')\\nlbl('Completion', 'Not observed in this filing (expected Q4 2016). Outside dates 12/31/2016, or 02/28/2017 if the only unsatisfied condition is STB approval. Expected closing kept separate from any observed closing.')\\nlbl('Termination fee', '$3,785,000 payable by the Company to G&W in specified cases (~3% of transaction value; the Company negotiated G&W\\\\u2019s draft down from 3.85%; Party B\\\\u2019s draft was 3% plus its transaction expenses capped at 1%).')\\nlbl('Filing identity and date', 'DEFM14A definitive proxy statement for the special meeting of shareholders (10/26/2016), filed 09/20/2016; background pages 27\\\\u201332. Source file: raw_filing/providence-worcester_2016-09-20_DEFM14A.htm.')\\nhead('3. Process and round map')\\nlbl('Processes', 'One sale process (Process 1). No earlier attempt is disclosed (the Q4 2015 Party A approach is round 0, not a separate process); no second process, go-shop or agreement termination is disclosed. Post-signing ledger content is publicity only (R057); the STB process and the 09/06/2016 BMO conflict confirmation sit in these Summary blocks.')\\nlbl('Round 0 (pre-solicitation)', 'R001 Party A interest (Q4 2015); R002 GHF adviser engaged (01/27/2016); R003 sale-strategy decision (03/14/2016); R004 Party A management meetings (03/22\\\\u201303/23); R005 contact authorization (03/24); R006 Hinckley Allen shown acting (03/24). No Round opened row for round 0.')\\nlbl('Round 1 (week of 03/28 \\\\u2013 06/01/2016)', 'R008 anchor = first outreach wave \\\\u2014 29 potential buyers contacted (R007); rejected candidate anchors R003 and R005. NDA wave R009\\\\u2013R011 (25 signers: 10 remaining strategic + 14 financial + G&W individually; no standstills). Access/differentiation: R012 (convention meetings), R013 (04/07 contact authorization), R014 (two additional Class I railroads contacted). Deadline history: R016 (05/10 set by 04/27), R017 (revised to 05/19), R018 (05/19; Enforced). Bids: R019 (nine IOIs, envelope $17.93\\\\u2013$26.50). Outcomes: R020 (16 residual non-submitters, inferred), R021 (06/01 decision), R022 (two low bidders dropped). Round-bidder tally: 9. Finality: Not final.')\\nlbl('Round 2 (mid-June \\\\u2013 07/27/2016)', 'R023 opened the LOI stage (due 07/20/2016; mark-ups and draft documents posted to the data site 06/29\\\\u201307/11). Late entrant Party C: R024 NDA, R025 IOI ($21.00), R026 catch-up access. Bids: R028\\\\u2013R032 (B $24.00, E $21.26, D $21.00, C $19.30, F $19.20) and R036\\\\u2013R037 (G&W $21.15, then $22.15). Deadline: R027 (07/20; Late bids accepted). Outcomes: R033\\\\u2013R034 (two non-submitters), R035 (Party A identity row), R038 (07/27 selection of G&W and Party B), R039\\\\u2013R042 (C, D, E, F dropped). Round-bidder tally: 6. Finality: Inferred final.')\\nlbl('Round 3 (07/27 \\\\u2013 08/12/2016)', 'R043 opened confirmatory due diligence and definitive negotiation with G&W and Party B. Re-entries R044\\\\u2013R045; bids R046\\\\u2013R048; withdrawal R049; access update R050; adviser R051; final bid R052 ($25.00); Board decision R053; signing R054; signing outcomes R055\\\\u2013R056. Round-bidder tally: 3. Finality: Inferred final.')\\nlbl('Post-signing', 'R057 announcement (08/15/2016); no competing proposal, go-shop activity, agreement termination or closing observed. Regulatory: STB petition for exemption filed 09/01/2016 and a voting-trust agreement submitted 09/14/2016 (X-009); outside dates X-010. Adviser conflict: on 09/06/2016 the Board considered BMO\\\\u2019s late disclosure of a ~5% BMO-affiliate lending participation in G&W\\\\u2019s secured syndicated facility and determined it was not material to BMO\\\\u2019s independence (P-029; X-016).')\\nhead('4. Participants and advisers')\\nlbl('G&W', 'Strategic (operating short-line/regional railroad; acquires through wholly owned shell Merger Sub). First observed 04/03/2016 (NDA R011; convention meeting R012); bids R036 ($21.15 with CVR), R037 ($22.15), R052 ($25.00 cash). Winner \\\\u2014 no exit row.')\\nlbl('Party A', 'Strategic (Class I rail partner). First observed Q4 2015 (R001); NDA within R009; memorandum recipient; never mentioned again \\\\u2192 Count-0 identity row R035 (Inferred: identity; possible covers R033 recommended, R020, R022). See Q4/Q5.')\\nlbl('Party B', 'Strategic. First individual meeting 04/21/2016 (R015); LOI R028 ($24.00); prioritized for definitive negotiation 08/04/2016; declined to raise on 08/12; Not selected at signing R055 (Would not improve earlier offer).')\\nlbl('Party C', 'Strategic late entrant. NDA R024 (early July); IOI R025 ($21.00); LOI R031 ($19.30); dropped R039 (07/27).')\\nlbl('Party D', 'Financial (as described in the filing). LOI R030 ($21.00); dropped R040; re-entered R044; revised LOI R046 ($24.00); Withdrew R049 (terms/process; no-sign commitment declined).')\\nlbl('Party E', 'Strategic. LOI R029 ($21.26); dropped R041; re-entered R045; revised LOI R047 ($23.81 with Party F financing); reversion R048 ($21.26); Not selected at signing R056.')\\nlbl('Party F', 'Strategic. LOI R032 ($19.20); dropped R042 (07/27 exit); provided financing support to Party E\\\\u2019s withdrawn 08/01 revised proposal (recorded on R047; no re-entry row after its exit).')\\nlbl('Anonymous cohorts', 'Two unnamed low bidders (Unknown type; dropped R022); one unnamed strategic and one unnamed financial non-submitter (R033, R034); 16 residual NDA signers closed by inference at 05/19/2016 (R020); two additional Class I railroads contacted before 04/07/2016 that never entered (R014). Cohorts are not extra parties to add to their members.')\\nlbl('Non-bidder holders', 'The Eder Trusts (shareholders; voting agreement 08/12/2016; X-012/X-024) and GATX Corporation (4.92% common holder; Director Smith recused from process meetings because GATX might be a potential buyer; no contact, NDA or bid disclosed) are not bidders and get no outcome rows.')\\nlbl('Advisers', 'GHF (Greene Holcomb & Fisher LLC) \\\\u2192 BMO Capital Markets Corp. \\\\u2014 Company financial adviser; engaged 01/27/2016 (R002); GHF\\\\u2019s business acquired by BMO 08/01/2016 (same relationship); aggregate fee ~$2.52 million (X-015); BMO-affiliate lending participation in G&W\\\\u2019s 2015 facility disclosed late and considered not material by the Board on 09/06/2016 (P-029; X-016). Hinckley, Allen & Snyder LLP \\\\u2014 Company legal counsel (R006; first shown acting 03/24/2016). Simpson Thacher & Bartlett LLP \\\\u2014 G&W legal counsel (R051; first shown acting 08/10/2016). The Company\\\\u2019s STB counsel is unnamed (P-026) and gets no adviser row. Disclosed attributes: PWRR and G&W are US public companies (NASDAQ: PWX; NYSE: GWR); ownership and country of the anonymous parties are not disclosed.')\\nhead('5. Counts and auction screen')\\nlbl('Auction screen', 'MET \\\\u2014 more than one independent prospective acquiring bidder unit executed bidder-target confidentiality agreements for this process (25 in the week-of-03/28 wave plus Party C; G&W among them). No lender-only, adviser or rollover-holder agreements are included; the Eder Trusts\\\\u2019 voting agreement is not a bidder NDA. Extraction proceeds regardless of the screen.')\\nlbl('Contacts (ledger tally)', \\\"=SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\\\\\\\"Contact\\\\\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\\\\\"Yes\\\\\\\")+SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\\\\\\\"Bidder interest\\\\\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\\\\\"Yes\\\\\\\")\\\")\\nlbl('  \\\\u2192 composition and filing assertions', '31 from Contact rows (29 in the GHF outreach wave + 2 additional Class I railroads approached by the Company) plus 1 from the Party A Bidder interest row, which carries the Q4 2015 first contact = 32 contact units. Party A\\\\u2019s 03/22\\\\u201303/23 meeting and Party B\\\\u2019s 04/21 meeting are Count 0 repeats. Filing: GHF contacted 11 potential strategic buyers and 18 potential financial buyers (29) in the week of 03/28/2016; the Company also approached two additional Class I railroads (P-004; P-006).')\\nlbl('NDA signers (ledger tally)', \\\"=SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\\\\\\\"NDA signed\\\\\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\\\\\"Yes\\\\\\\")\\\")\\nlbl('  \\\\u2192 filing assertions and reconciliation', 'Background: each of the 11 potential strategic buyers and 14 potential financial buyers executed confidentiality agreements (25), plus Party C\\\\u2019s early-July agreement = 26 signatures on the ledger\\\\u2019s reading; the Board\\\\u2019s reasons state \\\\u201c25 of whom entered into confidentiality agreements\\\\u201d (X-002). Q3 reconciles: the reasons\\\\u2019 25 may exclude Party C or one strategic signer.')\\nlbl('IOI submitters', '9 (stated; R019 cohort, envelope $17.93\\\\u2013$26.50; filing: \\\\u201cnine written indications of interest\\\\u201d, P-008).')\\nlbl('LOI submitters', '6 (stated; B, G&W, E, D, C, F \\\\u2014 R028\\\\u2013R032, R036; plus G&W\\\\u2019s 07/26 revision R037. Filing: \\\\u201csix LOIs\\\\u201d, P-012; group envelope $19.20\\\\u2013$24.00 / $96\\\\u2013121 million).')\\nlbl('Round-bidder tallies (R1 / R2 / R3)', \\\"=SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\\\\\\\"Bid\\\\\\\",'Deal ledger'!$F$3:$F$100,\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\\\\\"Yes\\\\\\\")&\\\\\\\" / \\\\\\\"&SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\\\\\\\"Bid\\\\\\\",'Deal ledger'!$F$3:$F$100,\\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\\\\\"Yes\\\\\\\")&\\\\\\\" / \\\\\\\"&SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\\\\\\\"Bid\\\\\\\",'Deal ledger'!$F$3:$F$100,\\\\\\\"3\\\\\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\\\\\"Yes\\\\\\\")\\\")\\nlbl('  \\\\u2192 scope', 'Bidder units newly represented as submitting in each round; not submissions and not unique bidders across the deal. R2 counts Party C\\\\u2019s IOI (R025) plus five LOIs; R3 counts D, E and G&W; later bids by the same bidder in the same round add 0 (G&W R037, C R031, E R048).')\\nlbl('Exit units and inferred share', \\\"=SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$AI$3:$AI$100,\\\\\\\"<>\\\\\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\\\\\"Yes\\\\\\\")&\\\\\\\" exit units; \\\\\\\"&SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$AJ$3:$AJ$100,\\\\\\\"Inferred: residual\\\\\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\\\\\"Yes\\\\\\\")&\\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\"&SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$AI$3:$AI$100,\\\\\\\"<>\\\\\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\\\\\"Yes\\\\\\\")&\\\\\\\" inferred by residual\\\\\\\"\\\")\\nlbl('  \\\\u2192 per-stage balance (Process 1)', 'R0/R1: 25 entrants \\\\u2212 16 inferred non-submitters (R020) \\\\u2212 2 low bidders (R022) = 7 continuing. R2: +1 (Party C, R024) \\\\u2212 2 non-submitters (R033\\\\u2013R034) \\\\u2212 4 dropped (R039\\\\u2013R042) = 2 continuing. R3: +2 re-entries (R044\\\\u2013R045) \\\\u2212 1 withdrawal (R049) \\\\u2212 2 signing outcomes (R055\\\\u2013R056) = 1 (winner). Total: 26 entrants + 2 re-entries \\\\u2212 27 exit units = 1. Party A\\\\u2019s Count-0 identity row (R035) moves no counts.')\\nlbl('  \\\\u2192 balance formula', \\\"=SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\\\\\\\"NDA signed\\\\\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\\\\\"Yes\\\\\\\")+SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\\\\\\\"Re-entered\\\\\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\\\\\"Yes\\\\\\\")-SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$AI$3:$AI$100,\\\\\\\"<>\\\\\\\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\\\\\\\"Yes\\\\\\\")\\\")\\nhead('6. Comparability and inputs')\\nlbl('Per-share basis', 'All offer prices are as-converted (preferred 100-for-1); the filing gives no decomposed per-share values except G&W\\\\u2019s cash/CVR split. All amounts are US dollars; no currency conversion attempted.')\\nlbl('Market benchmarks', 'Closing price 08/12/2016 (last trading day before announcement): $16.30 \\\\u2014 the $25.00 consideration is stated as a 53% premium (X-003). Closing price 09/16/2016: $24.88 (X-004). 2016 Q3 trading range through 09/16/2016: $15.60\\\\u2013$25.00 (X-005).')\\nlbl('Share counts and optional calculation', '4,866,593 common + 640 preferred (as-converted 64,000) = 4,930,593 as-converted shares on the 09/16/2016 record date; 53,368 options (18,368 vested) and 43,500 RSUs held by directors/officers (X-005; X-006). Optional labelled calculation (not filing-stated; excludes options/RSUs): $25.00 \\\\u00d7 4,930,593 = $123.26 million implied equity value.')\\nlbl('Contingent consideration', 'G&W\\\\u2019s July bids included a $1.13 per-share CVR tied to the subsequent sale of the South Quay property (book value $12.5 million used in BMO\\\\u2019s analyses); a contingent cash payment, so those bids remain All cash = Yes. The signed $25.00 terms exclude it.')\\nlbl('Other-scope proposals', 'None disclosed: every indication, LOI and final bid is for 100% of the outstanding common stock on an as-converted basis (P-009; P-016). No segment, asset or minority-stake proposals, so no Other-scope rows.')\\nlbl('Valuation statements (not bids)', 'BMO\\\\u2019s implied per-share reference ranges: selected companies $10.95\\\\u2013$14.56 and $11.42\\\\u2013$15.09; precedent transactions $10.54\\\\u2013$26.50; DCF $10.82\\\\u2013$12.34 \\\\u2014 each compared with the $25.00 consideration (X-017\\\\u2013X-019). These are adviser analyses, not offers, and are not entered in bid-price cells.')\\nlbl('Glossary', 'NDA = confidentiality agreement; IOI = indication of interest (non-binding); LOI = letter of intent (non-binding); CVR = contingent value right (extra cash tied to the South Quay property sale); confirmatory diligence = final-stage diligence after selection; data site = internet data room; exclusivity = a target commitment to deal only with one bidder (requested by several bidders; never granted); go-shop = post-signing solicitation period (none); STB = Surface Transportation Board; as-converted = treating preferred as converted 100-for-1 into common. Layout-only HTML decoding and whitespace normalization were applied to the filing text in the Source text sheet.')\\nlbl('Unverifiable items', 'Closing is not observed in this filing; the confidentiality-agreement count (25 vs 26) is reconciled in Q3; Party A\\\\u2019s later path is unresolved (Q5); no post-signing competition is disclosed.')\\n\\n# Questions\\nwsq = wb.create_sheet(QUESTIONS, 2)\\nfor c, name in enumerate(['Q','Review topic','Recommended answer','Why and source','Affected rows/fields','Consequence of changing it','Status','Reviewer note'], 1):\\n    cell = wsq.cell(row=1, column=c, value=name)\\n    cell.font = hdr_font; cell.fill = hdr_fill\\n    cell.alignment = Alignment(wrap_text=True, vertical='center')\\nQ = [\\n ('Q1', 'Process and round map, boundaries and finality',\\n  'Keep one process and three rounds: R1 anchored on the week-of-03/28/2016 first outreach wave (R008), R2 opened mid-June 2016 by the LOI instruction (R023), R3 opened 07/27/2016 by selection and the move to definitive negotiation (R043). Round 0 keeps the pre-solicitation items with no Round opened row. Finality: R1 Not final; R2 and R3 Inferred final. Keep the 04/03\\\\u201304/06 convention meetings as one Information access changed row (R012) and Party C\\\\u2019s catch-up access as one row (R026); keep the 08/09\\\\u201308/11 G&W continued-diligence grant as a Material process update (R050). Post-signing: publicity only (R057).',\\n  'The executed outreach is the preferred R1 anchor (P-004); rejected candidates R003 and R005 are retained as their own rows so the boundary can be moved. R2 alternative boundary 06/01/2016 (R021) rejected because no updated offers were sought then (P-008\\\\u2013P-009). R3 alternative boundaries 08/04 and 08/12 rejected because definitive negotiation with the selected bidders began on 07/27/2016 (P-020). R2 is Inferred final because the target moved to confirmatory due diligence and definitive negotiation at its close; R3 because it concluded with the executed agreement. Access rows follow section 4 (P-005; P-011); the 08/09 continued-diligence grant preceded G&W\\\\u2019s final bid (P-023).',\\n  'R003, R005, R007, R008, R012, R021, R023, R026, R038, R043, R050, R057; Round, Round finality, What happened',\\n  'Moving any boundary changes the round-bidder tallies (9/6/3) and the round map; reclassifying the access rows changes the access narrative but no counts.'),\\n ('Q2', 'Deadline history and treatments',\\n  'Record three versions: 05/10/2016 set by the 04/27/2016 board report (R016; superseded before arrival, no milestone row); revised to 05/19/2016 (R017; Extended) for the stated reason; 05/19/2016 reached while operative and treated Enforced (R018). The 07/20/2016 LOI due date (R023; R027) is treated Late bids accepted because G&W\\\\u2019s 07/21/2016 LOI and the other late-July LOIs were considered without a revision. G&W\\\\u2019s 6:00 p.m. 08/13/2016 offer expiry is not a bid deadline and stays in Terms (R052).',\\n  'Section 8.3 rules. The IOI receipt window 05/19\\\\u201306/01 straddles the due date, so no submission is late and Enforced (not Late bids accepted) applies (P-008). The revision reason is stated (P-007). The mid-June LOI instruction carries its due date on the R2 opening row, with the milestone row at 07/20/2016 (P-009; P-012; P-014).',\\n  'R016, R017, R018, R023 (Due date), R027, R052 (offer expiry in Terms); Deadline treatment, Due date, Date from/Date to of R017',\\n  'Changing treatments alters the Summary deadline map and the R2 narrative; treating the May IOIs as late would contradict the filing\\\\u2019s receipt window.'),\\n ('Q3', 'Confidentiality-agreement counts and auction screen',\\n  'Working total: 26 executed confidentiality agreements \\\\u2014 the 25 of the week-of-03/28 wave (11 strategic + 14 financial) plus Party C\\\\u2019s early-July agreement (R009\\\\u2013R011, R024). Read the Board\\\\u2019s reasons\\\\u2019 \\\\u201c25 of whom entered into confidentiality agreements\\\\u201d (X-002) as the reasons\\\\u2019 summary figure, most likely omitting Party C; alternatively the wave could have produced 24 signatures (10 strategic + 14 financial) with the total reaching 25 including Party C. Auction screen: met either way.',\\n  'Background supplies both specific statements: \\\\u201cEach of the potential strategic buyers and 14 potential financial buyers subsequently executed confidentiality agreements\\\\u201d and Party C\\\\u2019s separate agreement after its early-July approach (P-004; P-011). The reasons cite 25 (X-002). Section 3.2 prefers the specific background passages; the conflict is preserved here rather than silently resolved.',\\n  'R009, R010, R011, R024; Count cells; Summary \\\\u201cNDA signers\\\\u201d and auction screen',\\n  'If the total is 25 including Party C, R009 drops to 9 strategic signers and, if the submitter base stays 9, the inferred residual (R020) becomes 15 and the inferred share changes.'),\\n ('Q4', 'Inferred closures and per-stage balance',\\n  'Keep two inferred rows: R020 (Did not submit, Inferred: residual \\\\u2014 25 signers \\\\u2212 9 IOI submitters = 16, at the 05/19/2016 deadline) and R035 (Party A, Count 0, Inferred: identity, at 07/20/2016). All other outcomes are stated: two low bidders dropped 06/01 (R022), two LOI non-submitters (R033\\\\u2013R034), four 07/27 drops (R039\\\\u2013R042), one withdrawal (R049), two signing outcomes (R055\\\\u2013R056). Balance: R1 7 continuing; R2 2; R3 1 (winner); 16 of 27 exit units inferred.',\\n  'Section 10.2 arithmetic; base from P-004 (25 signers) and P-008 (9 submitters). The base is a stated exact number, so no bounds are needed; if the Q3 count changes, the residual changes by the same amount (flagged). R035 records only that Party A was out by the first named continuing set (P-012; P-020).',\\n  'R020, R022, R033, R034, R035, R039\\\\u2013R042, R049, R055, R056; Count, Outcome basis, Decided by, Exit reason',\\n  'Reclassifying any stated exit as inferred (or vice versa) changes the inferred-share arithmetic and balance; moving R035 to 05/19/2016 shifts its transition but no counts.'),\\n ('Q5', 'Identity mappings, anonymous cohorts and non-participants',\\n  'Recommended identities: the nine IOI submitters are Party B, G&W, Party D, Party E, Party F, the two unnamed low bidders and the two unnamed LOI non-submitters (one strategic, one financial). Party A is most likely the unnamed strategic LOI non-submitter (R033) and is placed at 07/20/2016 with Count 0; alternatives are the 16 residual non-submitters (R020, which would move it to 05/19) or a low bidder (R022). Party B\\\\u2019s 04/21 meeting and Party A\\\\u2019s 03/22\\\\u201303/23 meetings are repeats within the 29-buyer wave (Count 0). GATX\\\\u2019s possible-buyer recusal is not a participation event; the two additional Class I railroads never entered.',\\n  'Identifications follow the stage arithmetic (seven advancing = nine minus two low bidders; five of the seven plus Party C submitted LOIs) and the named LOI list (P-008; P-012; P-020). Party A\\\\u2019s last appearance is the memorandum recipient list (P-007). GATX recusal: P-020. Class I contacts: P-006.',\\n  'R014, R015, R019, R022, R033, R034, R035; Who, Count, Related rows; Summary participant list',\\n  'Re-identifying Party A (e.g., as a low bidder) would move its Count-0 row to R022 and change the reading of the two anonymous cohorts; no counts are asserted on this basis either way.'),\\n ('Q6', 'Formality, conditions and late-reconfirmation calls',\\n  'Formality: Formal for Party B (R028), G&W (R036\\\\u2013R037, R052) and Party D (R030, carried to R046) on returned agreement/voting-agreement mark-ups; Informal for the nine-IOI cohort (R019), Party C (R025, R031), Party E (R029, R047, R048) and Party F (R032) \\\\u2014 Party E\\\\u2019s issues summary is the borderline call (section 9.2 working default), flagged. Conditions: Heavy for the nine IOIs (pre-substantive-diligence context), C, D, E, F and G&W\\\\u2019s July LOIs (stated multi-week or exclusive diligence periods); Light for Party B (expedited review) and G&W\\\\u2019s 08/12 final bid (diligence completed; final documentation only; financing silent). No Bid reaffirmed row is recorded: Party B\\\\u2019s latest priced row is Formal and sits in an Inferred-final round, so the section 9.1 test fails; its 08/04 revised draft gets no row (further draft in the definitive stage).',\\n  'Formality signals/default: P-013/P-016/P-014 mark-ups and P-015 (issues summary) via P-012. Conditions tests: P-008, P-014\\\\u2013P-018, P-021, P-024. Late-reconfirmation conditions (a)\\\\u2013(c) with failure of (b): P-023; P-028.',\\n  'R019, R025\\\\u2013R032, R036\\\\u2013R037, R046\\\\u2013R048, R052, R055 (Formality, Conditions level, Conditions detail, Terms or outcome)',\\n  'Downgrading Party B or G&W to Informal changes the documentation profile but not prices or counts; upgrading Party E to Formal would make it a formal LOI, without changing selection.'),\\n ('Q7', 'Assigned Working dates that decide order',\\n  'Conventions used (all disclosed in Date method): R009\\\\u2013R010 03/28/2016 (signing-wave first day, Assigned: bound); R017 05/08/2016 (midpoint of the 04/27\\\\u201305/19 revision window); R019 05/19/2016 and R028\\\\u2013R032 07/20/2016 (solicitation due dates, Assigned: deadline); R039\\\\u2013R042 07/27/2016 (notifications after the decision, Assigned: decision day); R044\\\\u2013R045 07/29/2016. Within 08/12/2016 the order is G&W bid (morning) \\\\u2192 Board decision (afternoon) \\\\u2192 signing \\\\u2192 signing outcomes, per the stated sequence; the announcement follows on 08/15. R008 shares 03/28/2016 with R007/R009\\\\u2013R010 as a display tie.',\\n  'Section 8.1 rules 2\\\\u20136 and the order constraint; the May IOIs example (due date inside the receipt window) applies at R019. Same-day sequencing follows the filing\\\\u2019s own order (P-024; P-025; P-026; P-028).',\\n  'Date from, Date to, Working date, Date basis, Date method of R008\\\\u2013R010, R017, R019, R028\\\\u2013R032, R039\\\\u2013R042, R044\\\\u2013R045, R052\\\\u2013R056',\\n  'Changing an assigned date reorders rows (sorting is by Working date with # breaking ties) but not facts.'),\\n ('Q8', 'Comparability, consideration form and normalization',\\n  'Keep all per-share figures on the as-converted basis the filing used (P-008; P-009) and label the optional $123.26 million equity-value calculation as non-filing arithmetic. Classify G&W\\\\u2019s July cash-plus-CVR bids as All cash = Yes (contingent cash, not securities) with the $1.13 South Quay CVR and payoff trigger in Terms. Record no Other-scope bids (all proposals were for 100% of the common on an as-converted basis). Keep BMO\\\\u2019s implied reference ranges in Summary only, as valuation statements, never in bid-price cells.',\\n  'Consideration rules (section 9.4): P-014 for the CVR split and South Quay basis; P-005; P-009; P-012 for the as-converted basis; X-017\\\\u2013X-019 for the BMO ranges; X-005/X-006 for share counts. The $12.5 million South Quay book value is BMO\\\\u2019s input (financial analysis pages 38\\\\u201339).',\\n  'R019, R025\\\\u2013R032, R036\\\\u2013R037, R052, R054; Price kind/origin, Currency, All cash, Cash at closing; Summary comparability block',\\n  'Treating the CVR as non-cash would change All cash to No for the July G&W bids; entering BMO\\\\u2019s ranges as prices would create false observations \\\\u2014 both explicitly rejected above.'),\\n]\\nfor i, q in enumerate(Q, 2):\\n    for c, v in enumerate(q, 1):\\n        cell = wsq.cell(row=i, column=c, value=v)\\n        cell.alignment = Alignment(wrap_text=True, vertical='top')\\n    wsq.cell(row=i, column=1).font = Font(bold=True)\\n    wsq.cell(row=i, column=7).value = 'Pending'\\nfor col, w in zip('ABCDEFGH', [6, 34, 72, 72, 30, 42, 10, 18]):\\n    wsq.column_dimensions[col].width = w\\nwsq.freeze_panes = 'A2'\\nwsq.auto_filter.ref = f'A1:H{len(Q)+1}'\\n\\nassert wb.sheetnames.index(LEDGER) == 0 and wb.sheetnames.index(SUMMARY) == 1\\nassert wb.sheetnames.index(QUESTIONS) == 2 and wb.sheetnames.index(SOURCE) == 3\\nassert wb[LISTS].sheet_state == 'hidden' and len(wb.sheetnames) == 5\\nos.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT), exist_ok=True)\\nwb.save(OUT)\\nprint('saved', OUT)\\nprint('sheets:', wb.sheetnames)\\nprint('P rows', len(P_ROWS), 'X rows', len(X_ROWS))\\n\", \"path\": \"/tmp/opencode/build_workbook.py\"}"},"time":{"start":1789825127390,"end":1789825209831}}}}
