rred shares outstanding on the 09/16/2016 record date (preferred convertible 100-for-1; non-cumulative $5.00 dividend).\n[7] Focal acquirer and type :: Genesee & Wyoming Inc. (G&W), a Delaware corporation; NYSE: GWR; US public company; Strategic — operating short-line/regional railroad acquirer, buying through its wholly owned shell Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc. (formed 08/12/2016).\n[8] Agreed consideration :: $25.00 per share in cash (as-converted basis: preferred deemed converted into 100 common shares plus accrued and unpaid dividends); equity awards cashed out at $25.00 (options net of exercise price; RSUs at $25.00); no financing condition; G&W representation as to financial wherewithal. All cash: Yes. No CVR in the signed terms.\n[9] Signing :: 08/12/2016 — merger agreement among PWRR, G&W and Merger Sub; voting agreement among PWRR, G&W and the Eder Trusts (842,742 common shares, 500 preferred shares).\n[10] Announcement :: 08/15/2016 — Company press release before the opening of NASDAQ trading.\n[11] Completion :: Not observed in this filing (expected Q4 2016). Outside dates 12/31/2016, or 02/28/2017 if the only unsatisfied condition is STB approval. Expected closing kept separate from any observed closing.\n[12] Termination fee :: $3,785,000 payable by the Company to G&W in specified cases (~3% of transaction value; the Company negotiated G&W’s draft down from 3.85%; Party B’s draft was 3% plus its transaction expenses capped at 1%).\n[13] Filing identity and date :: DEFM14A definitive proxy statement for the special meeting of shareholders (10/26/2016), filed 09/20/2016; background pages 27–32. Source file: raw_filing/providence-worcester_2016-09-20_DEFM14A.htm.\n[14] 3. Process and round map :: None\n[15] Processes :: One sale process (Process 1). No earlier attempt is disclosed (the Q4 2015 Party A approach is round 0, not a separate process); no second process, go-shop or agreement termination is disclosed. Post-signing ledger content is publicity only (R057); the STB process and the 09/06/2016 BMO conflict confirmation sit in these Summary blocks.\n[16] Round 0 (pre-solicitation) :: R001 Party A interest (Q4 2015); R002 GHF adviser engaged (01/27/2016); R003 sale-strategy decision (03/14/2016); R004 Party A management meetings (03/22–03/23); R005 contact authorization (03/24); R006 Hinckley Allen shown acting (03/24). No Round opened row for round 0.\n[17] Round 1 (week of 03/28 – 06/01/2016) :: R008 anchor = first outreach wave — 29 potential buyers contacted (R007); rejected candidate anchors R003 and R005. NDA wave R009–R011 (25 signers: 10 remaining strategic + 14 financial + G&W individually; no standstills). Access/differentiation: R012 (convention meetings), R013 (04/07 contact authorization), R014 (two additional Class I railroads contacted). Deadline history: R016 (05/10 set by 0\n[18] Round 2 (mid-June – 07/27/2016) :: R023 opened the LOI stage (due 07/20/2016; mark-ups and draft documents posted to the data site 06/29–07/11). Late entrant Party C: R024 NDA, R025 IOI ($21.00), R026 catch-up access. Bids: R028–R032 (B $24.00, E $21.26, D $21.00, C $19.30, F $19.20) and R036–R037 (G&W $21.15, then $22.15). Deadline: R027 (07/20; Late bids accepted). Outcomes: R033–R034 (two non-submitters), R035 (Party A identity \n[19] Round 3 (07/27 – 08/12/2016) :: R043 opened confirmatory due diligence and definitive negotiation with G&W and Party B. Re-entries R044–R045; bids R046–R048; withdrawal R049; access update R050; adviser R051; final bid R052 ($25.00); Board decision R053; signing R054; signing outcomes R055–R056. Round-bidder tally: 3. Finality: Inferred final.\n[20] Post-signing :: R057 announcement (08/15/2016); no competing proposal, go-shop activity, agreement termination or closing observed. Regulatory: STB petition for exemption filed 09/01/2016 and a voting-trust agreement submitted 09/14/2016 (X-009); outside dates X-010. Adviser conflict: on 09/06/2016 the Board considered BMO’s late disclosure of a ~5% BMO-affiliate lending participation in G&W’s secured syndicated \n[21] 4. Participants and advisers :: None\n[22] G&W :: Strategic (operating short-line/regional railroad; acquires through wholly owned shell Merger Sub). First observed 04/03/2016 (NDA R011; convention meeting R012); bids R036 ($21.15 with CVR), R037 ($22.15), R052 ($25.00 cash). Winner — no exit row.\n[23] Party A :: Strategic (Class I rail partner). First observed Q4 2015 (R001); NDA within R009; memorandum recipient; never mentioned again → Count-0 identity row R035 (Inferred: identity; possible covers R033 recommended, R020, R022). See Q4/Q5.\n[24] Party B :: Strategic. First individual meeting 04/21/2016 (R015); LOI R028 ($24.00); prioritized for definitive negotiation 08/04/2016; declined to raise on 08/12; Not selected at signing R055 (Would not improve earlier offer).\n[25] Party C :: Strategic late entrant. NDA R024 (early July); IOI R025 ($21.00); LOI R031 ($19.30); dropped R039 (07/27).\n[26] Party D :: Financial (as described in the filing). LOI R030 ($21.00); dropped R040; re-entered R044; revised LOI R046 ($24.00); Withdrew R049 (terms/process; no-sign commitment declined).\n[27] Party E :: Strategic. LOI R029 ($21.26); dropped R041; re-entered R045; revised LOI R047 ($23.81 with Party F financing); reversion R048 ($21.26); Not selected at signing R056.\n[28] Party F :: Strategic. LOI R032 ($19.20); dropped R042 (07/27 exit); provided financing support to Party E’s withdrawn 08/01 revised proposal (recorded on R047; no re-entry row after its exit).\n[29] Anonymous cohorts :: Two unnamed low bidders (Unknown type; dropped R022); one unnamed strategic and one unnamed financial non-submitter (R033, R034); 16 residual NDA signers closed by inference at 05/19/2016 (R020); two additional Class I railroads contacted before 04/07/2016 that never entered (R014). Cohorts are not extra parties to add to their members.\n[30] Non-bidder holders :: The Eder Trusts (shareholders; voting agreement 08/12/2016; X-012/X-024) and GATX Corporation (4.92% common holder; Director Smith recused from process meetings because GATX might be a potential buyer; no contact, NDA or bid disclosed) are not bidders and get no outcome rows.\n[31] Advisers :: GHF (Greene Holcomb & Fisher LLC) → BMO Capital Markets Corp. — Company financial adviser; engaged 01/27/2016 (R002); GHF’s business acquired by BMO 08/01/2016 (same relationship); aggregate fee ~$2.52 million (X-015); BMO-affiliate lending participation in G&W’s 2015 facility disclosed late and considered not material by the Board on 09/06/2016 (P-029; X-016). Hinckley, Allen & Snyder LLP — Compa\n[32] 5. Counts and auction screen :: None\n[33] Auction screen :: MET — more than one independent prospective acquiring bidder unit executed bidder-target confidentiality agreements for this process (25 in the week-of-03/28 wave plus Party C; G&W among them). No lender-only, adviser or rollover-holder agreements are included; the Eder Trusts’ voting agreement is not a bidder NDA. Extraction proceeds regardless of the screen.\n[34] Contacts (ledger tally) :: =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\"Contact\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\"Yes\")+SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\"Bidder interest\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\"Yes\")\n[35]   → composition and filing assertions :: 31 from Contact rows (29 in the GHF outreach wave + 2 additional Class I railroads approached by the Company) plus 1 from the Party A Bidder interest row, which carries the Q4 2015 first contact = 32 contact units. Party A’s 03/22–03/23 meeting and Party B’s 04/21 meeting are Count 0 repeats. Filing: GHF contacted 11 potential strategic buyers and 18 potential financial buyers (29) in the week of \n[36] NDA signers (ledger tally) :: =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\"NDA signed\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\"Yes\")\n[37]   → filing assertions and reconciliation :: Background: each of the 11 potential strategic buyers and 14 potential financial buyers executed confidentiality agreements (25), plus Party C’s early-July agreement = 26 signatures on the ledger’s reading; the Board’s reasons state “25 of whom entered into confidentiality agreements” (X-002). Q3 reconciles: the reasons’ 25 may exclude Party C or one strategic signer.\n[38] IOI submitters :: 9 (stated; R019 cohort, envelope $17.93–$26.50; filing: “nine written indications of interest”, P-008).\n[39] LOI submitters :: 6 (stated; B, G&W, E, D, C, F — R028–R032, R036; plus G&W’s 07/26 revision R037. Filing: “six LOIs”, P-012; group envelope $19.20–$24.00 / $96–121 million).\n[40] Round-bidder tallies (R1 / R2 / R3) :: =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\"Bid\",'Deal ledger'!$F$3:$F$100,\"1\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\"Yes\")&\" / \"&SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\"Bid\",'Deal ledger'!$F$3:$F$100,\"2\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\"Yes\")&\" / \"&SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\"Bid\",'Deal ledger'!$F$3:$F$100,\"3\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\"Yes\")\n[41]   → scope :: Bidder units newly represented as submitting in each round; not submissions and not unique bidders across the deal. R2 counts Party C’s IOI (R025) plus five LOIs; R3 counts D, E and G&W; later bids by the same bidder in the same round add 0 (G&W R037, C R031, E R048).\n[42] Exit units and inferred share :: =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$AI$3:$AI$100,\"<>\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\"Yes\")&\" exit units; \"&SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$AJ$3:$AJ$100,\"Inferred: residual\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\"Yes\")&\"/\"&SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$AI$3:$AI$100,\"<>\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\"Yes\")&\" inferred by residual\"\n[43]   → per-stage balance (Process 1) :: R0/R1: 25 entrants − 16 inferred non-submitters (R020) − 2 low bidders (R022) = 7 continuing. R2: +1 (Party C, R024) − 2 non-submitters (R033–R034) − 4 dropped (R039–R042) = 2 continuing. R3: +2 re-entries (R044–R045) − 1 withdrawal (R049) − 2 signing outcomes (R055–R056) = 1 (winner). Total: 26 entrants + 2 re-entries − 27 exit units = 1. Party A’s Count-0 identity row (R035) moves no counts.\n[44]   → balance formula :: =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\"NDA signed\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\"Yes\")+SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$D$3:$D$100,\"Re-entered\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\"Yes\")-SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$3:$Q$100,'Deal ledger'!$AI$3:$AI$100,\"<>\",'Deal ledger'!$P$3:$P$100,\"Yes\")\n[45] 6. Comparability and inputs :: None\n[46] Per-share basis :: All offer prices are as-converted (preferred 100-for-1); the filing gives no decomposed per-share values except G&W’s cash/CVR split. All amounts are US dollars; no currency conversion attempted.\n[47] Market benchmarks :: Closing price 08/12/2016 (last trading day before announcement): $16.30 — the $25.00 consideration is stated as a 53% premium (X-003). Closing price 09/16/2016: $24.88 (X-004). 2016 Q3 trading range through 09/16/2016: $15.60–$25.00 (X-005).\n[48] Share counts and optional calculation :: 4,866,593 common + 640 preferred (as-converted 64,000) = 4,930,593 as-converted shares on the 09/16/2016 record date; 53,368 options (18,368 vested) and 43,500 RSUs held by directors/officers (X-005; X-006). Optional labelled calculation (not filing-stated; excludes options/RSUs): $25.00 × 4,930,593 = $123.26 million implied equity value.\n[49] Contingent consideration :: G&W’s July bids included a $1.13 per-share CVR tied to the subsequent sale of the South Quay property (book value $12.5 million used in BMO’s analyses); a contingent cash payment, so those bids remain All cash = Yes. The signed $25.00 terms exclude it.\n[50] Other-scope proposals :: None disclosed: every indication, LOI and final bid is for 100% of the outstanding common stock on an as-converted basis (P-009; P-016). No segment, asset or minority-stake proposals, so no Other-scope rows.\n[51] Valuation statements (not bids) :: BMO’s implied per-share reference ranges: selected companies $10.95–$14.56 and $11.42–$15.09; precedent transactions $10.54–$26.50; DCF $10.82–$12.34 — each compared with the $25.00 consideration (X-017–X-019). These are adviser analyses, not offers, and are not entered in bid-price cells.\n[52] Glossary :: NDA = confidentiality agreement; IOI = indication of interest (non-binding); LOI = letter of intent (non-binding); CVR = contingent value right (extra cash tied to the South Quay property sale); confirmatory diligence = final-stage diligence after selection; data site = internet data room; exclusivity = a target commitment to deal only with one bidder (requested by several bidders; never granted);\n[53] Unverifiable items :: Closing is not observed in this filing; the confidentiality-agreement count (25 vs 26) is reconciled in Q3; Party A’s later path is unresolved (Q5); no post-signing competition is disclosed.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"[1] PWRR × G&W — deal ledger summary (Providence and Worcester Railroad Company / Genesee & Wyoming Inc., 2016) :: None\n[2] 1. Status and commercial account :: None\n[3] Delivery status :: AI first pass; not human-approved. Instruction: SEC_Deal_Ledger_Extraction_Instruction.md, revision of 19 September 2026 (short form). Supplied source: providence-worcester_2016-09-20_DEFM14A.htm — PWRR definitive proxy statement (DEFM14A) filed 09/20/2016, proxy dated 09/19/2016. Source coverage: the complete “Background of the Merger” (pp. 27–32) is reproduced in order in the Source text sheet (\n[4] Commercial account :: Initiation was mixed: a Q4 2015 approach by a Class I rail partner (Party A) expressing interest in acquiring equity led, through the Board’s banker search and its 03/14/2016 decision to explore a change of control, to a bro