{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825333366,"sessionID":"ses_f4628b113ffe9gyXGlLM5DZwK2","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e735ab0016K4LEJUUTrYQy3","sessionID":"ses_f4628b113ffe9gyXGlLM5DZwK2","messageID":"msg_0b9e72adf0016goFeDikEDTCzG","type":"tool","id":"call_00_HZhF1QvYuyB1g4EoTeOb2050","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode && python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\nwb=load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx')\nwsq=wb['Questions']\nfor r in range(1, wsq.max_row+1):\n    print('=== ['+str(r)+']', wsq.cell(r,1).value, '|', wsq.cell(r,2).value, '| status:', wsq.cell(r,7).value)\n    for c in (3,4,5,6):\n        v=str(wsq.cell(r,c).value)\n        print('   -', wsq.cell(1,c).value, ':', v[:220])\nEOF"},"output":"=== [1] Q | Review topic | status: Status\n   - Recommended answer : Recommended answer\n   - Why and source : Why and source\n   - Affected rows/fields : Affected rows/fields\n   - Consequence of changing it : Consequence of changing it\n=== [2] Q1 | Process and round map, boundaries and finality | status: Pending\n   - Recommended answer : Keep one process and three rounds: R1 anchored on the week-of-03/28/2016 first outreach wave (R008), R2 opened mid-June 2016 by the LOI instruction (R023), R3 opened 07/27/2016 by selection and the move to definitive neg\n   - Why and source : The executed outreach is the preferred R1 anchor (P-004); rejected candidates R003 and R005 are retained as their own rows so the boundary can be moved. R2 alternative boundary 06/01/2016 (R021) rejected because no updat\n   - Affected rows/fields : R003, R005, R007, R008, R012, R021, R023, R026, R038, R043, R050, R057; Round, Round finality, What happened\n   - Consequence of changing it : Moving any boundary changes the round-bidder tallies (9/6/3) and the round map; reclassifying the access rows changes the access narrative but no counts.\n=== [3] Q2 | Deadline history and treatments | status: Pending\n   - Recommended answer : Record three versions: 05/10/2016 set by the 04/27/2016 board report (R016; superseded before arrival, no milestone row); revised to 05/19/2016 (R017; Extended) for the stated reason; 05/19/2016 reached while operative a\n   - Why and source : Section 8.3 rules. The IOI receipt window 05/19–06/01 straddles the due date, so no submission is late and Enforced (not Late bids accepted) applies (P-008). The revision reason is stated (P-007). The mid-June LOI instru\n   - Affected rows/fields : R016, R017, R018, R023 (Due date), R027, R052 (offer expiry in Terms); Deadline treatment, Due date, Date from/Date to of R017\n   - Consequence of changing it : Changing treatments alters the Summary deadline map and the R2 narrative; treating the May IOIs as late would contradict the filing’s receipt window.\n=== [4] Q3 | Confidentiality-agreement counts and auction screen | status: Pending\n   - Recommended answer : Working total: 26 executed confidentiality agreements — the 25 of the week-of-03/28 wave (11 strategic + 14 financial) plus Party C’s early-July agreement (R009–R011, R024). Read the Board’s reasons’ “25 of whom entered \n   - Why and source : Background supplies both specific statements: “Each of the potential strategic buyers and 14 potential financial buyers subsequently executed confidentiality agreements” and Party C’s separate agreement after its early-J\n   - Affected rows/fields : R009, R010, R011, R024; Count cells; Summary “NDA signers” and auction screen\n   - Consequence of changing it : If the total is 25 including Party C, R009 drops to 9 strategic signers and, if the submitter base stays 9, the inferred residual (R020) becomes 15 and the inferred share changes.\n=== [5] Q4 | Inferred closures and per-stage balance | status: Pending\n   - Recommended answer : Keep two inferred rows: R020 (Did not submit, Inferred: residual — 25 signers − 9 IOI submitters = 16, at the 05/19/2016 deadline) and R035 (Party A, Count 0, Inferred: identity, at 07/20/2016). All other outcomes are st\n   - Why and source : Section 10.2 arithmetic; base from P-004 (25 signers) and P-008 (9 submitters). The base is a stated exact number, so no bounds are needed; if the Q3 count changes, the residual changes by the same amount (flagged). R035\n   - Affected rows/fields : R020, R022, R033, R034, R035, R039–R042, R049, R055, R056; Count, Outcome basis, Decided by, Exit reason\n   - Consequence of changing it : Reclassifying any stated exit as inferred (or vice versa) changes the inferred-share arithmetic and balance; moving R035 to 05/19/2016 shifts its transition but no counts.\n=== [6] Q5 | Identity mappings, anonymous cohorts and non-participants | status: Pending\n   - Recommended answer : Recommended identities: the nine IOI submitters are Party B, G&W, Party D, Party E, Party F, the two unnamed low bidders and the two unnamed LOI non-submitters (one strategic, one financial). Party A is most likely the u\n   - Why and source : Identifications follow the stage arithmetic (seven advancing = nine minus two low bidders; five of the seven plus Party C submitted LOIs) and the named LOI list (P-008; P-012; P-020). Party A’s last appearance is the mem\n   - Affected rows/fields : R014, R015, R019, R022, R033, R034, R035; Who, Count, Related rows; Summary participant list\n   - Consequence of changing it : Re-identifying Party A (e.g., as a low bidder) would move its Count-0 row to R022 and change the reading of the two anonymous cohorts; no counts are asserted on this basis either way.\n=== [7] Q6 | Formality, conditions and late-reconfirmation calls | status: Pending\n   - Recommended answer : Formality: Formal for Party B (R028), G&W (R036–R037, R052) and Party D (R030, carried to R046) on returned agreement/voting-agreement mark-ups; Informal for the nine-IOI cohort (R019), Party C (R025, R031), Party E (R02\n   - Why and source : Formality signals/default: P-013/P-016/P-014 mark-ups and P-015 (issues summary) via P-012. Conditions tests: P-008, P-014–P-018, P-021, P-024. Late-reconfirmation conditions (a)–(c) with failure of (b): P-023; P-028.\n   - Affected rows/fields : R019, R025–R032, R036–R037, R046–R048, R052, R055 (Formality, Conditions level, Conditions detail, Terms or outcome)\n   - Consequence of changing it : Downgrading Party B or G&W to Informal changes the documentation profile but not prices or counts; upgrading Party E to Formal would make it a formal LOI, without changing selection.\n=== [8] Q7 | Assigned Working dates that decide order | status: Pending\n   - Recommended answer : Conventions used (all disclosed in Date method): R009–R010 03/28/2016 (signing-wave first day, Assigned: bound); R017 05/08/2016 (midpoint of the 04/27–05/19 revision window); R019 05/19/2016 and R028–R032 07/20/2016 (so\n   - Why and source : Section 8.1 rules 2–6 and the order constraint; the May IOIs example (due date inside the receipt window) applies at R019. Same-day sequencing follows the filing’s own order (P-024; P-025; P-026; P-028).\n   - Affected rows/fields : Date from, Date to, Working date, Date basis, Date method of R008–R010, R017, R019, R028–R032, R039–R042, R044–R045, R052–R056\n   - Consequence of changing it : Changing an assigned date reorders rows (sorting is by Working date with # breaking ties) but not facts.\n=== [9] Q8 | Comparability, consideration form and normalization | status: Pending\n   - Recommended answer : Keep all per-share figures on the as-converted basis the filing used (P-008; P-009) and label the optional $123.26 million equity-value calculation as non-filing arithmetic. Classify G&W’s July cash-plus-CVR bids as All \n   - Why and source : Consideration rules (section 9.4): P-014 for the CVR split and South Quay basis; P-005; P-009; P-012 for the as-converted basis; X-017–X-019 for the BMO ranges; X-005/X-006 for share counts. The $12.5 million South Quay \n   - Affected rows/fields : R019, R025–R032, R036–R037, R052, R054; Price kind/origin, Currency, All cash, Cash at closing; Summary comparability block\n   - Consequence of changing it : Treating the CVR as non-cash would change All cash to No for the July G&W bids; entering BMO’s ranges as prices would create false observations — both explicitly rejected above.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== [1] Q | Review topic | status: Status\n   - Recommended answer : Recommended answer\n   - Why and source : Why and source\n   - Affected rows/fields : Affected rows/fields\n   - Consequence of changing it : Consequence of changing it\n=== [2] Q1 | Process and round map, boundaries and finality | status: Pending\n   - Recommended answer : Keep one process and three rounds: R1 anchored on the week-of-03/28/2016 first outreach wave (R008), R2 opened mid-June 2016 by the LOI instruction (R023), R3 opened 07/27/2016 by selection and the move to definitive neg\n   - Why and source : The executed outreach is the preferred R1 anchor (P-004); rejected candidates R003 and R005 are retained as their own rows so the boundary can be moved. R2 alternative boundary 06/01/2016 (R021) rejected because no updat\n   - Affected rows/fields : R003, R005, R007, R008, R012, R021, R023, R026, R038, R043, R050, R057; Round, Round finality, What happened\n   - Consequence of changing it : Moving any boundary changes the round-bidder tallies (9/6/3) and the round map; reclassifying the access rows changes the access narrative but no counts.\n=== [3] Q2 | Deadline history and treatments | status: Pending\n   - Recommended answer : Record three versions: 05/10/2016 set by the 04/27/2016 board report (R016; superseded before arrival, no milestone row); revised to 05/19/2016 (R017; Extended) for the stated reason; 05/19/2016 reached while operative a\n   - Why and source : Section 8.3 rules. The IOI receipt window 05/19–06/01 straddles the due date, so no submission is late and Enforced (not Late bids accepted) applies (P-008). The revision reason is stated (P-007). The mid-June LOI instru\n   - Affected rows/fields : R016, R017, R018, R023 (Due date), R027, R052 (offer expiry in Terms); Deadline treatment, Due date, Date from/Date to of R017\n   - Consequence of changing it : Changing treatments alters the Summary deadline map and the R2 narrative; treating the May IOIs as late would contradict the filing’s receipt window.\n=== [4] Q3 | Confidentiality-agreement counts and auction screen | status: Pending\n   - Recommended answer : Working total: 26 executed confidentiality agreements — the 25 of the week-of-03/28 wave (11 strategic + 14 financial) plus Party C’s early-July agreement (R009–R011, R024). Read the Board’s reasons’ “25 of whom entered \n   - Why and source : Background supplies both specific statements: “Each of the potential strategic buyers and 14 potential financial buyers subsequently executed confidentiality agreements” and Party C’s separate agreement after its early-J\n   - Affected rows/fields : R009, R010, R011, R024; Count cells; Summary “NDA signers” and auction screen\n   - Consequence of changing it : If the total is 25 including Party C, R009 drops to 9 strategic signers and, if the submitter base stays 9, the inferred residual (R020) becomes 15 and the inferred share changes.\n=== [5] Q4 | Inferred closures and per-stage balance | status: Pending\n   - Recommended answer : Keep two inferred rows: R020 (Did not submit, Inferred: residual — 25 signers − 9 IOI submitters = 16, at the 05/19/2016 deadline) and R035 (Party A, Count 0, Inferred: identity, at 07/20/2016). All other outcomes are st\n   - Why and source : Section 10.2 arithmetic; base from P-004 (25 signers) and P-008 (9 submitters). The base is a stated exact number, so no bounds are needed; if the Q3 count changes, the residual changes by the same amount (flagged). R035\n   - Affected rows/fields : R020, R022, R033, R034, R035, R039–R042, R049, R055, R056; Count, Outcome basis, Decided by, Exit reason\n   - Consequence of changing it : Reclassifying any stated exit as inferred (or vice versa) changes the inferred-share arithmetic and balance; moving R035 to 05/19/2016 shifts its transition but no counts.\n=== [6] Q5 | Identity mappings, anonymous cohorts and non-participants | status: Pending\n   - Recommended answer : Recommended identities: the nine IOI submitters are Party B, G&W, Party D, Party E, Party F, the two unnamed low bidders and the two unnamed LOI non-submitters (one strategic, one financial). Party A is most likely the u\n   - Why and source : Identifications follow the stage arithmetic (seven advancing = nine minus two low bidders; five of the seven plus Party C submitted LOIs) and the named LOI list (P-008; P-012; P-020). Party A’s last appearance is the mem\n   - Affected rows/fields : R014, R015, R019, R022, R033, R034, R035; Who, Count, Related rows; Summary participant list\n   - Consequence of changing it : Re-identifying Party A (e.g., as a low bidder) would move its Count-0 row to R022 and change the reading of the two anonymous cohorts; no counts are asserted on this basis either way.\n=== [7] Q6 | Formality, conditions and late-reconfirmation calls | status: Pending\n   - Recommended answer : Formality: Formal for Party B (R028), G&W (R036–R037, R052) and Party D (R030, carried to R046) on returned agreement/voting-agreement mark-ups; Informal for the nine-IOI cohort (R019), Party C (R025, R031), Party E (R02\n   - Why and source : Formality signals/default: P-013/P-016/P-014 mark-ups and P-015 (issues summary) via P-012. Conditions tests: P-008, P-014–P-018, P-021, P-024. Late-reconfirmation conditions (a)–(c) with failure of (b): P-023; P-028.\n   - Affected rows/fields : R019, R025–R032, R036–R037, R046–R048, R052, R055 (Formality, Conditions level, Conditions detail, Terms or outcome)\n   - Consequence of changing it : Downgrading Party B or G&W to Informal changes the documentation profile but not prices or counts; upgrading Party E to Formal would make it a formal LOI, without changing selection.\n=== [8] Q7 | Assigned Working dates that decide order | status: Pending\n   - Recommended answer : Conventions used (all disclosed in Date method): R009–R010 03/28/2016 (signing-wave first day, Assigned: bound); R017 05/08/2016 (midpoint of the 04/27–05/19 revision window); R019 05/19/2016 and R028–R032 07/20/2016 (so\n   - Why and source : Section 8.1 rules 2–6 and the order constraint; the May IOIs example (due date inside the receipt window) applies at R019. Same-day sequencing follows the filing’s own order (P-024; P-025; P-026; P-028).\n   - Affected rows/fields : Date from, Date to, Working date, Date basis, Date method of R008–R010, R017, R019, R028–R032, R039–R042, R044–R045, R052–R056\n   - Consequence of changing it : Changing an assigned date reorders rows (sorting is by Working date with # breaking ties) but not facts.\n=== [9] Q8 | Comparability, consideration form and normalization | status: Pending\n   - Recommended answer : Keep all per-share figures on the as-converted basis the filing used (P-008; P-009) and label the optional $123.26 million equity-value calculation as non-filing arithmetic. Classify G&W’s July cash-plus-CVR bids as All \n   - Why and source : Consideration rules (section 9.4): P-014 for the CVR split and South Quay basis; P-005; P-009; P-012 for the as-converted basis; X-017–X-019 for the BMO ranges; X-005/X-006 for share counts. The $12.5 million South Quay \n   - Affected rows/fields : R019, R025–R032, R036–R037, R052, R054; Price kind/origin, Currency, All cash, Cash at closing; Summary comparability block\n   - Consequence of changing it : Treating the CVR as non-cash would change All cash to No for the July G&W bids; entering BMO’s ranges as prices would create false observations — both explicitly rejected above.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Command exited with code 0."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /tmp/opencode && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\\nwb=load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx')\\nwsq=wb['Questions']\\nfor r in range(1, wsq.max_row+1):\\n    print('=== ['+str(r)+']', wsq.cell(r,1).value, '|', wsq.cell(r,2).value, '| status:', wsq.cell(r,7).value)\\n    for c in (3,4,5,6):\\n        v=str(wsq.cell(r,c).value)\\n        print('   -', wsq.cell(1,c).value, ':', v[:220])\\nEOF\"}"},"time":{"start":1789825332651,"end":1789825333366}}}}
