{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825356513,"sessionID":"ses_f4628b113ffe9gyXGlLM5DZwK2","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e78f5800166U20rlTg8iLGU","sessionID":"ses_f4628b113ffe9gyXGlLM5DZwK2","messageID":"msg_0b9e77bb2001GbkFFKXaYzIRJ1","type":"tool","id":"call_00_sZoszOFjeBK5I8lH0lBi7647","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode && python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\nwb=load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx')\nws=wb['Deal ledger']\nfor rid in ['R011','R020','R035','R047','R054']:\n    r=[x for x in range(3,ws.max_row+1) if ws.cell(x,15).value==rid][0]\n    print('####', rid)\n    print('WHEN:', ws.cell(r,2).value)\n    print('WHO:', ws.cell(r,3).value, '| TYPE:', ws.cell(r,7).value)\n    print('TERMS:', ws.cell(r,8).value)\n    print('WHY:', ws.cell(r,11).value)\n    print('SOURCE:', ws.cell(r,12).value)\n    print('PAGE:', ws.cell(r,37).value, '| REL:', ws.cell(r,38).value)\n    print()\nEOF"},"output":"#### R011\nWHEN: 04/03/2016\nWHO: G&W (Genesee & Wyoming Inc.) | TYPE: Strategic\nTERMS: Acquisition-related confidentiality agreement between the Company and G&W dated 04/03/2016 (the merger agreement’s defined “Confidentiality Agreement”); G&W also met management at the 2016 Connections Convention (04/03–04/06) and received the memorandum.\nWHY: NDA signed (stated): the merger agreement definition fixes G&W’s individual date and the wave cohort rows (R009–R010) exclude it. Quotes: “shall mean the Confidentiality Agreement between the Company and Parent dated April 3, 2016” / “including Party A, Party B and G&W, that had executed confidentiality agreements”\nSOURCE: =HYPERLINK(\"#Source text!$D$31\",\"X-001; P-007 (main: X-001)\")\nPAGE: A-48 | REL: R009/R010 (wave cohorts)\n\n#### R020\nWHEN: by 05/19/2016\nWHO: 16 remaining NDA signers (of the 25) | TYPE: Unknown\nTERMS: Inferred: residual — 25 NDA signers (11 strategic + 14 financial) − 9 IOI submitters = 16 non-submitters at the 05/19/2016 IOI deadline. Includes the wave’s silent signers never individually mentioned again; Party A may also sit here (see R035). Type: Unknown — type split of the residual is not supplied.\nWHY: Inferred: residual (section 10.2). Base: “Each of the potential strategic buyers and 14 potential financial buyers subsequently executed confidentiality agreements” (25); accounted submitters: nine IOIs (R019). No other stated exits, and the next transition names the continuing seven as all within the nine. Supporting quote: “Between May 19, 2016 and June 1, 2016, the Company received nine written indications of interest”.\nSOURCE: =HYPERLINK(\"#Source text!$D$5\",\"P-004; P-008 (main: P-004)\")\nPAGE: 28 | REL: base R009–R011; covered submitters R019\n\n#### R035\nWHEN: by 07/20/2016\nWHO: Party A (identity row) | TYPE: Strategic\nTERMS: Inferred: identity — Party A is not among the six named LOI submitters, the first continuing set the filing identifies by name; the row records only that Party A was out by this transition, not which anonymous exit was its own. Count 0. Covering cohorts that could already count it: R033 (unnamed strategic LOI non-submitter — recommended reading), R020 (16 residual non-submitters, which would place it at 05/19/2016), R022 (two low bidders). See Q4/Q5. No counts moved from a cohort to this name.\nWHY: Inferred: identity (section 10.2): Party A is introduced in Q4 2015, named among the memorandum recipients, and never mentioned again; the first named continuing set without it is the six LOI submitters: “In late July 2016, the Company received six LOIs with offer prices per share ranging from $19.20 to $24.00” (P-012). Other quotes: “including Party A, Party B and G&W, that had executed confidentiality agreements” / “proceed with confirmatory due diligence and negotiations with G&W and Party B because of the higher offers made by each of G&W and Party B relative to the other potential buyers”\nSOURCE: =HYPERLINK(\"#Source text!$D$8\",\"P-007; P-012; P-020 (main: P-007)\")\nPAGE: 28 | REL: None\n\n#### R047\nWHEN: 08/01/2016\nWHO: Party E | TYPE: Strategic\nTERMS: Support: Party F (financing) — revised LOI at $23.81 per share (as-converted; point) with a 30-day due diligence period, submitted along with financing support from Party F (which had exited on 07/27/2016; no re-entry row and no independent bid by Party F after its exit). First Party E bid in Round 3 (Count 1).\nWHY: Bid (stated price revision with a disclosed financing-support relationship; section 5.3 records support on the supported bidder’s offer row). Quotes: “Party E submitted a revised LOI, along with financing support, from Party F, at a price of $23.81 per share” / “Both revised proposals contained a 30-day due diligence period” Formality: carries forward Party E’s Informal status (issues summary; no markup returned) — flagged Q6. Conditions: 30-day diligence period → Heavy.\nSOURCE: =HYPERLINK(\"#Source text!$D$22\",\"P-021 (main: P-021)\")\nPAGE: 30 | REL: revises R029; supporter exited at R042 (no re-entry); support ended with R048\n\n#### R054\nWHEN: 08/12/2016\nWHO: PWRR, G&W and Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc. | TYPE: None\nTERMS: Executed the merger agreement (Merger Sub merges into PWRR, which survives as a wholly owned G&W subsidiary; $25.00 cash per common share; preferred converted 100-for-1 plus accrued dividends; equity awards cashed out) and, with the Eder Trusts, the voting agreement (842,742 common / 500 preferred; ~17.3% / 78.1% of record-date class shares). Company termination fee $3,785,000 (~3% of transaction value; G&W draft negotiated down from 3.85%; Party B’s draft was 3% plus expenses capped at 1%); no financing condition; outside dates 12/31/2016, or 02/28/2017 if only STB approval remains. Signing is not a bid row: agreed consideration stated here, price/formality/conditionality cells left blank.\nWHY: Merger agreement signed (stated). Quotes: “the Company and G&W executed the merger agreement, and the Company, G&W and the Eder Trusts executed the voting agreement” / “shall mean $3,785,000” Fee history: “termination fee equal to 3% of the transaction value in the case of G&W (which the Company had negotiated down from 3.85%” Outside date: “if the merger is not completed by December 31, 2016 (or, if the only unsatisfied condition is STB approval of the merger, by February 28, 2017” Financing condition: “the absence of a financing condition in the merger agreement and the representation of G&W in the merger agreement as to its financial wherewithal” Termination-fee and fiduciary-out terms were consequential for selection and are folded into this row (section 4).\nSOURCE: =HYPERLINK(\"#Source text!$D$29\",\"P-028; X-023; X-010; P-025; X-022 (main: P-028)\")\nPAGE: 32 | REL: Board approval R053\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"#### R011\nWHEN: 04/03/2016\nWHO: G&W (Genesee & Wyoming Inc.) | TYPE: Strategic\nTERMS: Acquisition-related confidentiality agreement between the Company and G&W dated 04/03/2016 (the merger agreement’s defined “Confidentiality Agreement”); G&W also met management at the 2016 Connections Convention (04/03–04/06) and received the memorandum.\nWHY: NDA signed (stated): the merger agreement definition fixes G&W’s individual date and the wave cohort rows (R009–R010) exclude it. Quotes: “shall mean the Confidentiality Agreement between the Company and Parent dated April 3, 2016” / “including Party A, Party B and G&W, that had executed confidentiality agreements”\nSOURCE: =HYPERLINK(\"#Source text!$D$31\",\"X-001; P-007 (main: X-001)\")\nPAGE: A-48 | REL: R009/R010 (wave cohorts)\n\n#### R020\nWHEN: by 05/19/2016\nWHO: 16 remaining NDA signers (of the 25) | TYPE: Unknown\nTERMS: Inferred: residual — 25 NDA signers (11 strategic + 14 financial) − 9 IOI submitters = 16 non-submitters at the 05/19/2016 IOI deadline. Includes the wave’s silent signers never indiv