{"type":"text","timestamp":1789825445667,"sessionID":"ses_f4628b113ffe9gyXGlLM5DZwK2","part":{"id":"prt_0b9e8d15c001RuO5GMdq6MfQp3_text-0","sessionID":"ses_f4628b113ffe9gyXGlLM5DZwK2","messageID":"msg_0b9e8d15c001RuO5GMdq6MfQp3","type":"text","text":"The workbook is built and checked. Deliverable: **`/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx`** — four visible sheets (Deal ledger, Summary, Questions, Source text) plus the hidden Lists sheet, 57 ledger rows, 29 background paragraphs + 24 supporting passages in Source text.\n\n## The sale, in plain language\nProvidence & Worcester (PWRR, Worcester MA; NASDAQ: PWX) began through a Q4 2015 approach by a Class I rail partner (\"Party A\") that expressed interest in acquiring equity. After the Board hired GHF (Greene Holcomb & Fisher, later BMO) and approved an exploratory process on 03/14/2016, its banker contacted 29 buyers (11 strategic, 18 financial) in the week of 03/28/2016; 25 signed no-standstill NDAs. Nine non-binding IOIs arrived 05/19–06/01 at $17.93–$26.50/share as-converted; the two weakest were cut and seven went to management presentations and a data site. The mid-June LOI round (due 07/20, with mark-ups) drew six LOIs in late July ($19.20–$24.00): Party B led at $24.00 and G&W at $21.15 (cash plus a $1.13 South Quay CVR), then $22.15. On 07/27 the committee picked G&W and Party B for confirmatory diligence and definitive negotiation and told the rest they were out; D and E briefly re-engaged (08/01 revised LOIs; E supported by F financing) but D withdrew 08/02 and E reverted to $21.26. On 08/12 G&W's final $25.00 all-cash LOI (CVR dropped, mark-ups returned, 6:00 p.m. next-day expiry) beat B after B refused to raise, and the Board signed the same day; announcement 08/15. Observed outcome: signed merger agreement, no go-shop, no post-signing competing proposal, closing not observed (expected Q4 2016; STB petition 09/01, voting-trust submission 09/14).\n\n## Most consequential review items (details in the Questions sheet)\n1. **Round map (Q1).** One process, three rounds: R1 anchored on the week-of-03/28 outreach (R008; rejected anchors R003/R005 kept as rows), R2 mid-June LOI stage (R023), R3 07/27 definitive negotiation (R043). R2 and R3 are \"Inferred final\", R1 \"Not final\". The convention meetings (R012) and Party C's catch-up access (R026) are kept as single access rows per section 4.\n2. **NDA count conflict (Q3).** Background gives 11+14 = 25 wave signers plus Party C = 26; the Board's reasons say 25. Recommended: 26 signatures, the reasons' 25 excluding Party C — flagged for the researcher.\n3. **Inferred closures (Q4).** Two inferred rows only: 16 residual non-submitters (25 − 9, at 05/19) and Party A's Count-0 identity row at 07/20 (Q5 covers its possible covers: recommended the unnamed strategic LOI non-submitter; alternatives R020/R022).\n4. **Formality/conditions (Q6).** Party E's issues summary kept Informal (borderline); G&W/B/D Formal on mark-ups; Heavy conditions for the stated multi-week/exclusive diligence bids; no late-reconfirmation row (Party B fails the round-finality test).\n5. **Deadlines (Q2)** and **assigned working dates that decide order (Q7)** — grouped in one question each.\n\n## What I could not verify / limitations\n- **Closing is not observed** in this filing; the transaction outcome recorded is signing + announcement.\n- **Party A's actual path** (whether it bid, was a low bidder, or never submitted) is unresolvable from the filing; recorded as an inferred-identity row, not a fabricated history.\n- **Formula recalculation and hyperlink behavior were not executed in a spreadsheet engine here** (LibreOffice crashes in this sandbox). The eight Summary formulas (SUMIFS-based tallies, exit/inferred split, balance) were verified by independent arithmetic against the ledger (contacts 32, NDA 26, round tallies 9/6/3, exits 27 with 16 inferred, balance 1); the Source cells are `=HYPERLINK(\"#Source text!$D$n\", ...)` local links and the 15 drop-down validations reference the Lists sheet (warning-level enforcement), but I could not open the file in Excel/LibreOffice to confirm rendering.\n- Annex-sourced rows carry the annex page label \"A-48\" in the Page field (no numeric page exists in the filing). Non-decreasing working dates, unique row ids, controlled-value conformance, and quote recoverability from the Source text were all checked programmatically.","time":{"start":1789825438050,"end":1789825445667}}}
